      "comment": "Allocates memory with 16-byte alignment for SIMD/cache optimization.\n\nThis is RAD Game Tools' custom memory allocator wrapper that ensures returned \npointers are aligned to 16-byte boundaries. It stores the alignment offset in \nthe byte immediately preceding the returned pointer to enable proper freeing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input size is non-zero and not -1 (invalid sentinel)\n2. Add 16 bytes to requested size for alignment overhead\n3. Call AllocateMemoryWithRetry to get raw memory block\n4. If allocation fails, return NULL (0)\n5. Calculate alignment: bAlignmentPadding = 16 - (pRawBlock & 0x0F)\n6. Compute aligned pointer: pAlignedBlock = pRawBlock + bAlignmentPadding\n7. Store padding byte at pAlignedBlock[-1] for radfree to recover original pointer\n8. Return aligned pointer\n\nParameters:\n  nSize - Requested allocation size in bytes. Must be > 0 and != -1.\n\nReturns:\n  Success: Pointer to 16-byte aligned memory block\n  Failure: NULL (0) if nSize is 0, -1, or allocation fails\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10 (16) - Alignment boundary and overhead added to allocation\n  0x0F (15) - Mask to extract low 4 bits for alignment calculation\n  -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) - Invalid size sentinel value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - nSize == 0: Returns NULL immediately\n  - nSize == -1: Returns NULL (treated as invalid sentinel)\n  - Underlying allocation failure: Returns NULL\n\nMemory Layout:\n  [raw_block] ... [padding_byte] [aligned_user_memory...]\n                   ^              ^\n                   |              +-- Returned pointer (16-byte aligned)\n                   +-- Stores padding count (1-16) for radfree",
