      "name": "SendCopyData",
      "signature": "LRESULT SendCopyData(HWND hWnd, WPARAM wParam, uint dwData, uint dwDataSize, void * pDataBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "LRESULT",
      "comment": "Sends data to another window using WM_COPYDATA inter-process communication.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy COPYDATASTRUCT fields (dwData, dwDataSize, pDataBuffer) to stack\n2. Build pointer to stack-based COPYDATASTRUCT\n3. Send WM_COPYDATA (0x4a) via SendMessageA\n4. Return result from SendMessageA\n\nParameters:\n  hWnd         - HWND: Target window handle to receive the message\n  wParam       - WPARAM: Handle to window passing the data (sender)\n  dwData       - uint: Application-defined data identifier (COPYDATASTRUCT.dwData)\n  dwDataSize   - uint: Size in bytes of data pointed to by pDataBuffer (COPYDATASTRUCT.cbData)\n  pDataBuffer  - void*: Pointer to data buffer to be copied (COPYDATASTRUCT.lpData)\n\nReturns:\n  LRESULT: Return value from target window's message handler\n           TRUE if data was processed, FALSE otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x4a - WM_COPYDATA message constant\n\nStructure Layout (COPYDATASTRUCT built on stack):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type    Description\n  0x0     4     dwData        uint    Application-defined value\n  0x4     4     cbData        uint    Size of data in lpData\n  0x8     4     lpData        void*   Pointer to data buffer\n\nNotes:\n  - Stack-based struct avoids heap allocation\n  - Data is copied by Windows during SendMessage\n  - Commonly used for IPC between windows/processes",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:864ac812e1ffe3bfa8d2899c021bd9ad9a393cdb924a50f74d35c48f6e47a311",
