      "name": "_SmackBufferString@8",
      "signature": "char * _SmackBufferString@8(int pSmackBuffer, char * szOutputBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Builds a descriptive string describing the Smack video buffer type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Determine buffer type string based on SmackBuffer.type field (offset 0x8)\n2. If type is 5 (DIBSection) and DIB support available, use \"DIBSection\"\n3. Otherwise lookup type name from PTR_s_Automatic table by type index\n4. Copy the type string to the output buffer using inline strcpy loop\n5. Check if accelerated blitting is enabled (offsets 0x484 and 0x48c non-zero)\n6. If enabled, find end of current string using SCASB.REPNE\n7. Append \" with accelerated blitting (\" suffix (28 bytes via MOVSD.REP)\n8. Call SmackBlitString to append blit method description\n9. Append closing parenthesis \")\" from g_wCloseParenSuffix\n10. Return pointer to output buffer\n\nParameters:\npSmackBuffer - Pointer to SmackBuffer structure containing video buffer info\n  +0x008: dwBufferType - Buffer type enum (0=Automatic, 1=WinG, 5=DIBSection)\n  +0x484: pBlitHandler - Accelerated blit handler (non-zero if enabled)\n  +0x48c: dwBlitFlags - Secondary blit flag (must be non-zero for suffix)\nszOutputBuffer - Destination buffer for the descriptive result string\n\nReturns:\nchar* - Returns szOutputBuffer pointer for function call chaining\n\nSpecial Cases:\nDIBSection (type 5) only selected when g_pfnSetDIBColorTable is initialized\nAccelerated blitting suffix requires BOTH +0x484 AND +0x48c to be non-zero",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:ed8855673ec21b917fb4fee869577813",
