      "name": "HandleWindowMessage",
      "signature": "int HandleWindowMessage(int nHwnd, uint dwMsg, int nWParam, int nLParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Window message handler for focus management on F5 key.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if message is WM_SYSCOMMAND (0x112)\n  2. Check if wParam has F5 key code (0xF120 mask match)\n  3. If match: Set focus to window at offset 0x470 in global struct\n  4. Otherwise: Delegate to original window procedure at offset 0x468\n\nParameters:\n  hwnd       HWND - Window handle\n  uMsg       UINT - Message code (0x112 = WM_SYSCOMMAND)\n  wParam     int  - Message parameter (F5 = 0xF120)\n  lParam     LPARAM - Additional message parameter\n\nReturns:\n  0 on successful F5 key handling (focus set)\n  Result from CallWindowProcA for all other messages\n\nNotes:\n  Global data at 0x10015e8c contains window procedure table\n  Offset 0x470: Window handle for focus target\n  Offset 0x468: Original WNDPROC function pointer\ndwNewLong parameter of SetWindowLongA\n",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:a85c08f6f487d71093b25d65b9d5885d42db46cdb9d0594803b896b6b56f1e4d",
