      "name": "HandleActivateMessage",
      "signature": "LRESULT HandleActivateMessage(HWND hWnd, UINT uMsg, WPARAM wParam, LPARAM lParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "LRESULT",
      "comment": "Handles WM_ACTIVATE (0x6) messages for window state management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if message is WM_ACTIVATE (0x6)\n  2. Forward message to child window via SendMessageA with custom message 0x5a78\n  3. If activating (wParam != 0): Set flag at offset 0x460, call original procedure\n  4. If state field at offset 0x8 equals 3, copy 64000 bytes between buffers\n  5. If deactivating (wParam == 0): Clear flag, optionally copy buffers if state == 3\n  6. For all other messages: Delegate to original window procedure\n\nParameters:\n  hWnd (HWND): Handle to window receiving the message\n  uMsg (UINT): Message identifier (WM_ACTIVATE = 0x6)\n  wParam (WPARAM): Activation state (0 = deactivating, non-zero = activating)\n  lParam (LPARAM): Additional message context\n\nReturns:\n  LRESULT: Result from CallWindowProcA or 0 after buffer copy\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x6      - WM_ACTIVATE message code\n  0x5a78   - Custom application message forwarded to child window\n  0xfa00   - 64000 bytes buffer copy size\n  3        - State value triggering buffer swap operations\n\nStructure Layout (g_pApplicationContext offsets):\n  0x008: int    - State flag controlling buffer operations\n  0x448: byte*  - Primary buffer pointer\n  0x44c: byte*  - Secondary buffer pointer\n  0x460: uint   - Activation state flag (1=active, 0=inactive)\n  0x464: HWND   - Child window for message forwarding\n  0x46c: WNDPROC - Original window procedure",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
