      "name": "SmackBufferOpen",
      "signature": "uint * SmackBufferOpen(HWND hWnd, uint dwFlags, uint dwWidth, uint dwHeight, uint dwScaledWidth, uint dwScaledHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint *",
      "comment": "Opens and initializes a Smack video buffer for rendering video frames to a window.\n\nThis function creates the rendering infrastructure needed to display Smacker video\ncontent, supporting multiple rendering backends (WinG, DIB, DirectDraw) based on\nsystem capabilities and requested flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize display globals if first call (color depth, palette size, Windows version)\n2. Determine reserved palette entries based on system palette usage\n3. Calculate scaling requirements and check if scaling is needed\n4. Select rendering mode based on flags and system capabilities:\n   - Mode 2: DisplayDib (320x240 max)\n   - Mode 3: DisplayDib variant (320x200 max)\n   - Mode 4: Mode 13h emulation with 64KB buffer\n   - Mode 5: DIB section rendering\n   - Mode 6: WinG/DirectDraw accelerated rendering (preferred)\n5. Allocate SmackBuffer structure (0x4BC bytes = 1212 bytes)\n6. Initialize buffer fields with dimensions, color depth, and scaling info\n7. Create rendering surface (bitmap/DirectDraw surface)\n8. Set up palette entries from system palette if 8-bit mode\n9. Create child window for display if windowed mode\n10. Return pointer to initialized SmackBuffer\n\nParameters:\n  hWnd - Parent window handle for rendering context\n  dwFlags - Buffer creation flags:\n    0x80: Force software cursor mode\n    0x100: Use bilinear scaling\n    0x200: Use point sampling scaling\n    Bits 0-6: Preferred rendering mode (0=auto)\n  dwWidth - Native video frame width in pixels\n  dwHeight - Native video frame height in pixels\n  dwScaledWidth - Display width (0 = same as dwWidth)\n  dwScaledHeight - Display height (0 = same as dwHeight)\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to SmackBuffer structure on success\n  NULL on failure (allocation failed, DC creation failed, or no suitable renderer)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x4BC (1212) - SmackBuffer structure size\n  0x12F (303) - Number of DWORDs to clear in buffer\n  0x100 (256) - Standard 8-bit palette size\n  0x18 (24) - Maximum color depth cap (24-bit)\n  0x141 (321) - DisplayDib max width + 1\n  0xF1 (241) - DisplayDib max height + 1 (mode 2)\n  0xC9 (201) - DisplayDib max height + 1 (modes 3-4)\n  0x140 (320) - Mode 13h width\n  0xC8 (200) - Mode 13h height\n  0xFA00 (64000) - Mode 13h buffer size (320*200)\n\nError Handling:\n  - Returns NULL if radmalloc fails for buffer allocation\n  - Returns NULL if DC creation fails (WinG/GDI)\n  - Returns NULL if DIB section creation fails\n  - Calls ApplyPresetUnitTileAttributes to cleanup on failure\n  - Falls through rendering modes on capability failure",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:038ba4be67f3c71e1a1c68e3e9a8936e",
