      "name": "InitializeDibSupport",
      "signature": "void InitializeDibSupport(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize DIB (Device-Independent Bitmap) support by loading GDI32 functions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if already initialized via g_dwDibInitialized flag\n  2. If already initialized, return early\n  3. Mark initialization flag (0x1) to prevent re-initialization\n  4. Get OS version via GetVersion() to validate platform capability\n  5. Mask version to 0x800000ff and check if Windows NT (0x80000003)\n  6. If not NT, return (DIB not available on Win9x)\n  7. Load \"GDI32\" module handle via GetModuleHandleA()\n  8. Get SetDIBColorTable function pointer and store in g_pfnSetDIBColorTable\n  9. Get CreateDIBSection function pointer and store in g_pfnCreateDIBSection\n  10. Exit with success\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Pre-allocates function pointers to NULL\n  - Only functions on Windows NT (not Win95/98/ME)\n  - Initialization guarded by atomic flag to prevent race conditions\n  - Silently exits if platform doesn't support DIB rendering",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:f4b191709540b351caef618b0aa84553",
