      "name": "InitializeWinGLibrary",
      "signature": "void InitializeWinGLibrary(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes the WinG graphics library for legacy Windows 3.1 compatibility.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Set error mode to SEM_NOOPENFILEERRORBOX (0x8000) to suppress DLL load errors\n  2. Call InitializeDibSupport (FUN_10001d50) to check for native GDI32 DIB support\n  3. If GDI32 SetDIBColorTable is not available (g_pfnSetDIBColorTable == 0),\n     load WING32.DLL as fallback\n  4. Restore original error mode\n  5. If module handle > 0x1F (valid), resolve 6 WinG function pointers via GetProcAddress\n  6. If load failed, set g_hWinGModule to 0x1 as failure marker\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results stored in global function pointers:\n    g_pfnWinGCreateDC        (0x10015898)\n    g_pfnWinGCreateBitmap    (0x10015890)\n    g_pfnWinGBitBlt          (0x100158a8)\n    g_pfnWinGStretchBlt      (0x100158a4)\n    g_pfnWinGRecommendDIBFormat (0x1001588c)\n    g_pfnWinGSetDIBColorTable   (0x10015ce0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Module handle <= 0x1F indicates LoadLibrary failure (error codes)\n  - Sets g_hWinGModule = 0x1 on failure to mark initialization attempted\n  - Skips WING32.DLL load if GDI32 already has SetDIBColorTable (Win95+)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
