      "name": "InitDisplayDibWindowClass",
      "signature": "bool InitDisplayDibWindowClass(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Initializes the DisplayDib window class for display operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Save current error mode with SetErrorMode(0x8000)\n  2. Load DISPDIB.DLL module using LoadModule\n  3. Restore previous error mode\n  4. If module loaded successfully (handle > 0x1f):\n     5. Query DisplayDibWindow class info via GetClassInfoA\n     6. Return class info query result (true if found)\n  7. Return false if module load failed\n\nParameters:\n  None (initialization function)\n\nReturns:\n  true if DisplayDibWindow class was successfully registered\n  false if DISPDIB.DLL failed to load or class not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Error mode temporarily set to 0x8000 to suppress error dialogs during module load\n  - Threshold comparison (0x1f/31) used to verify valid module handle\n  - Only GetClassInfoA is called if module load succeeds",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
