      "name": "BlitSmackBufferToScreen",
      "signature": "dword BlitSmackBufferToScreen(int * pSmackBuf, HDC hdcDest, int nDestX, int nDestY, dword dwSrcX, dword dwSrcY, dword dwWidth, dword dwHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "BlitSmackBufferToScreen - Renders a Smack video buffer to a device context with optional clipping and scaling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pSmackBuf pointer; return 0 if NULL\n2. Check blit mode at offset +0x4A4 (2 = multiple blit queue mode)\n3. If multiple blit mode and queue not full:\n   - Queue blit parameters to batch buffer at +0x4AC\n   - Store HDC at +0x4B8, increment queue count at +0x4B4\n   - Return 0 (deferred blit)\n4. Set dirty flag at +0x444 to mark buffer as modified\n5. Check if GDI mode (+0x8 != 3) or DirectDraw mode (+0xC != 0)\n6. If hdcDest is NULL, get DC from buffer's window handle (+0x464)\n7. Select and realize palette from buffer (+0x458)\n8. Handle full palette update flag (+0x440) if set\n9. Check clip mode (+0x484):\n   - If clipping enabled and first blit flag set:\n     - Convert client coords to screen via ClientToScreen\n     - Verify window visible via IsWindowVisible\n     - Check if window is foreground or child of foreground\n     - Update clip region at +0x48C-0x4A0\n10. If stretching mode (+0x1C != 0):\n    - Use StretchBlt or StretchDIBits based on flags\n    - Calculate scaled dimensions from source and dest ratios\n11. Otherwise use BitBlt for 1:1 copy\n12. If DirectDraw surface mode:\n    - Handle surface locking via IDirectDrawSurface vtable\n    - Call SmackBlit for software rendering\n13. Handle cursor hiding via SmackCheckCursor/SmackRestoreCursor\n14. Restore original palette, release DC if acquired internally\n15. Return status code (0 = success, 0x100 = error/refresh needed)\n\nParameters:\n  pSmackBuf (int*): Pointer to SmackBuffer structure containing video state\n  hdcDest (HDC): Destination device context, or NULL to use window DC\n  nDestX (int): Destination X coordinate in pixels\n  nDestY (int): Destination Y coordinate in pixels\n  dwSrcX (dword): Source X offset within video buffer\n  dwSrcY (dword): Source Y offset within video buffer\n  dwWidth (dword): Width of region to blit\n  dwHeight (dword): Height of region to blit\n\nReturns:\n  0x000 - Success, blit completed\n  0x100 - Error or refresh required (palette changed, window moved)\n\nStructure Layout (SmackBuffer at pSmackBuf):\n  Offset  Size  Field                 Description\n  0x008   4     dwBlitMode            Blit method (3=GDI, 4=StretchDIB, 5=Direct)\n  0x00C   4     dwUseDirectDraw       DirectDraw enabled flag\n  0x010   4     dwVideoWidth          Source video width\n  0x014   4     dwVideoHeight         Source video height\n  0x018   4     dwBitsPerPixel        Color depth (8, 16, 24, 32)\n  0x01C   4     dwStretchMode         Stretch scaling enabled\n  0x020   4     dwScaledWidth         Scaled destination width\n  0x024   4     dwScaledHeight        Scaled destination height\n  0x440   4     fFullPaletteUpdate    Force full palette refresh\n  0x444   4     fBufferDirty          Buffer modified flag\n  0x448   4     pVideoData            Pointer to raw pixel data\n  0x458   4     hPalette              GDI palette handle\n  0x45C   4     hdcMem                Memory DC for buffer\n  0x464   4     hWnd                  Associated window handle\n  0x47C   4     pDirectDrawSurface    IDirectDrawSurface pointer\n  0x480   4     dwSurfaceFlags        Surface capability flags\n  0x484   4     fClipEnabled          Screen clipping enabled\n  0x488   4     fSmoothScale          Smooth scaling hint\n  0x48C   4     fClipRegionValid      Clip region initialized\n  0x490   4     fNeedsFullRefresh     Full redraw required\n  0x494   16    rcClipRect            Clipping rectangle (RECT)\n  0x4A4   4     dwBlitQueueMode       0=immediate, 1=process queue, 2=queuing\n  0x4AC   4     pBlitQueuePtr         Current queue write pointer\n  0x4B0   4     dwMaxQueuedBlits      Maximum blits in queue\n  0x4B4   4     dwQueuedBlitCount     Current queued blit count\n  0x4B8   4     hdcQueued             HDC for queued blits\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x42        - BLACKNESS ROP for PatBlt (black fill)\n  0xCC0020    - SRCCOPY ROP for BitBlt/StretchBlt\n  0x30        - SPI_GETWORKAREA for SystemParametersInfo\n  0x3         - COLORONCOLOR for SetStretchBltMode\n  0x887601C2  - DDERR_SURFACELOST DirectDraw error code",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
