      "name": "_SmackBufferNewPalette@12",
      "signature": "void _SmackBufferNewPalette@12(int * pSmackBuf, byte * pbPaletteData, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Updates the color palette for a SmackBuffer video playback structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer and mark palette as dirty (offset 0x444)\n2. Check if palette has more than 255 colors (offset 0x2c)\n3. Copy existing palette entries to local LOGPALETTE structure\n4. Calculate color channel offsets based on flags:\n   - Bit 0: 16-bit mode (double all offsets)\n   - Bit 1: Swap red and blue channels\n   - Bit 2: Use 4-byte stride\n   - Bit 3: Alternative BGR ordering\n5. Process each palette entry from source data:\n   - Read RGB values at calculated offsets\n   - Check for color collisions with existing entries\n   - Adjust red component by +/-1 to avoid exact duplicates\n   - Store in both local palette and buffer palette (offset 0x3c)\n6. Create or update Windows palette:\n   - If using DIB (offset 0xc == 0): DeleteObject old, CreatePalette new\n   - If DIB mode 5: Update via SetDIBColorTable or WinG API\n   - Otherwise: Call InitializePaletteBuffer\n7. Mark for redraw if high-color (offset 0x28 > 256)\n8. Update SmackBlit context palette if present (offset 0x484)\n\nParameters:\n  pSmackBuf - SmackBuffer structure pointer containing palette at offset 0x3c\n  pbPaletteData - Source palette data (RGB triplets or quads based on flags)\n  dwFlags - Color format flags:\n            Bit 0 (0x1): 16-bit color mode (double offsets)\n            Bit 1 (0x2): Swap R/B channels\n            Bit 2 (0x4): Use 4-byte stride\n            Bit 3 (0x8): BGR ordering with 4-byte stride\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Layout (SmackBuffer offsets):\n  Offset | Size | Field           | Description\n  0x08   | 4    | dwBlitMode      | Blit mode (5 = DIB)\n  0x0C   | 4    | fUseDIB         | Non-zero if using DIB section\n  0x28   | 4    | dwColorDepth    | Color depth (>256 = high color)\n  0x2C   | 4    | dwPaletteSize   | Number of palette entries\n  0x34   | 4    | dwPaletteStart  | First palette index to process\n  0x38   | 4    | dwPaletteEnd    | Last palette index to process\n  0x3C   | 1024 | abPalette       | Raw palette data (256 * 4 bytes)\n  0x43C  | 4    | dwPaletteFlags  | Palette format flags\n  0x440  | 4    | fNeedsRedraw    | Redraw required flag\n  0x444  | 4    | fPaletteDirty   | Palette modified flag\n  0x458  | 4    | hPalette        | HPALETTE handle\n  0x45C  | 4    | hDC             | Device context for DIB\n  0x484  | 4    | pBlitContext    | SmackBlitContext pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x300 - LOGPALETTE version number (Windows 3.0)\n  0x100 - Maximum palette entries (256)\n  0x04  - peFlags value for PC_RESERVED palette entry",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
