      "name": "_SmackBufferClose@4",
      "signature": "void _SmackBufferClose@4(int pSmackBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Closes and releases all resources associated with a Smacker video buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return immediately if pSmackBuffer is NULL\n2. Switch on buffer type (offset +0x8):\n   - Type 1-3: Free buffer data pointer at +0x448 or +0x44c\n   - Type 4: Free buffer data, skip to common cleanup\n   - Type 5 (GDI mode): Release GDI objects and DirectDraw surfaces\n3. For types 1-3, hide and close associated window if present\n4. Common cleanup: Free auxiliary buffer at +0x4a8, delete palette object at +0x458\n5. Free the SmackBuffer structure itself\n\nParameters:\n  pSmackBuffer - Pointer to SmackBuffer structure to close, or NULL (no-op)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nBuffer Type Values:\n  1-3: Memory buffer modes (different data pointer offsets)\n  4: Simple memory buffer (no window)\n  5: GDI/DirectDraw mode with device context and surfaces\n\nStructure Offsets (SmackBuffer):\n  +0x008: dwBufferType - Buffer rendering mode\n  +0x448: pBufferData - Primary buffer pointer (types 1-4)\n  +0x44c: pAltBuffer - Alternate buffer pointer (type 3)\n  +0x450: hBitmap - GDI bitmap handle\n  +0x454: hOldBitmap - Original bitmap for SelectObject restore\n  +0x458: hPalette - Palette object handle\n  +0x45c: hDC - Device context handle\n  +0x470: hWnd - Associated window handle\n  +0x478: pDDSurface1 - DirectDraw surface interface 1\n  +0x47c: pDDSurface2 - DirectDraw surface interface 2\n  +0x484: pDDClipper - DirectDraw clipper interface\n  +0x4a8: pAuxBuffer - Auxiliary data buffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x402: WM_USER + 2 - Custom message to signal buffer closure",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:8e91ad4803a0a3757e2e7308558e950db3b6d97a9693a2e32bfd0de68c762d5c",
