      "name": "_SmackBufferFromScreen@16",
      "signature": "void _SmackBufferFromScreen@16(int * pSmackBuffer, HWND hWnd, short nScreenX, short nScreenY)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Captures screen content from a window and stores it into a SmackBuffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pSmackBuffer is not null\n2. If hWnd is provided and valid, convert client coordinates to screen coordinates via ClientToScreen\n3. Get device context for the screen (null hWnd for desktop DC)\n4. Build LOGPALETTE from system palette entries, setting PC_RESERVED flag (0x04) for entries within the buffer's palette range [nPaletteStartIndex, nPaletteEndIndex)\n5. Create and realize palette on both screen DC and compatible DC\n6. Create compatible bitmap matching SmackBuffer dimensions (width at offset 0x18, height at offset 0x14)\n7. BitBlt screen region to compatible bitmap using SRCCOPY (0xCC0020)\n8. Initialize SmackBuffer globals; negate height if buffer format flag is 0\n9. Extract DIB bits into SmackBuffer's pixel data area (offset 0x448)\n10. Restore original palettes, delete created GDI objects\n11. Copy 256-entry global palette buffer to SmackBuffer at offset 0x3C\n12. Reset global palette buffer to identity mapping (0-255)\n\nParameters:\n  pSmackBuffer - Pointer to SmackBuffer structure receiving captured screen data\n  hWnd - Window handle for coordinate conversion; NULL to use raw screen coordinates\n  nScreenX - X coordinate (client coords if hWnd valid, else screen coords)\n  nScreenY - Y coordinate (client coords if hWnd valid, else screen coords)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; SmackBuffer is populated with screen capture data\n\nSmackBuffer Structure Layout (partial):\n  Offset  Size  Field               Description\n  0x00    4     dwFormatFlag        0 = flip height negative for DIB\n  0x14    2     wHeight             Buffer height in pixels\n  0x18    2     wWidth              Buffer width in pixels\n  0x2C    4     dwPaletteEntries    Number of palette entries (typically 256)\n  0x34    4     dwPaletteStart      First reserved palette index\n  0x38    4     dwPaletteEnd        Last reserved palette index + 1\n  0x3C    1024  aPalette            256-entry palette array (4 bytes each)\n  0x448   4     pPixelData          Pointer to DIB pixel buffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x300 - LOGPALETTE version (Windows 3.0 format)\n  0x04 - PC_RESERVED flag for palette entry\n  0xCC0020 - SRCCOPY raster operation\n  0x100 - 256 palette entries",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:cdd884237f99492e7d1bd575d913e7970e755a2e2804857d55370af7215fd71a",
