      "name": "CopySmackBufferPalette",
      "signature": "void CopySmackBufferPalette(int pDestBuffer, int pSrcSmack, int nUseColorMatch)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Copies palette data from a source Smack video to a destination SmackBuffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pDestBuffer and pSrcSmack pointers; exit early if NULL\n2. If nUseColorMatch is non-zero, perform color-matching palette remapping:\n   a. For each of 256 destination palette entries (outer loop at 0x10003bc7):\n      - Initialize dwMinDistance to 0x7FFFFFFF (max int)\n      - For each of 256 source palette entries (inner loop at 0x10003bd4):\n        - Calculate RGB color distance: (R1-R2)^2 + (G1-G2)^2 + (B1-B2)^2\n        - If distance < dwMinDistance, update best match index\n        - Exit inner loop early if exact match found (distance=0)\n      - Store best matching source index in remap table\n   b. Apply remapping to pixel buffer rows using lookup table\n3. Copy 256 RGBQUAD palette entries (0x400 bytes) from source to destination\n4. If destination has existing GDI palette object, delete it via DeleteObject\n5. Clear the palette object handle in destination buffer\n\nParameters:\npDestBuffer - SmackBuffer* - Destination buffer to receive palette data\npSrcSmack - Smack* - Source Smack structure containing palette at offset 0x3C\nnUseColorMatch - int - If non-zero, remap palette by finding closest color matches\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; palette copied in-place to destination buffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x3C - Offset to palette data within Smack/SmackBuffer structures\n0x100 - Number of palette entries (256 colors)\n0x40C - Offset to pixel data pointer in SmackBuffer\n0x458 - Offset to GDI palette handle in SmackBuffer\n0x7FFFFFFF - Initial minimum distance (max signed 32-bit integer)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
