      "name": "_SmackBufferClear@8",
      "signature": "void _SmackBufferClear@8(int pSmackBuf, byte bFillValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Clears a SmackBuffer by filling all rows with a specified byte value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pSmackBuf is not NULL\n2. Get pointer to buffer data from SmackBuffer+0x448\n3. Loop through each row (0 to height-1):\n   a. Get row width from SmackBuffer+0x10\n   b. Fill row using optimized DWORD writes (REP STOSD)\n   c. Fill remaining bytes with single-byte writes (REP STOSB)\n   d. Advance row pointer by stride (SmackBuffer+0x18)\n\nParameters:\n  pSmackBuf - Pointer to SmackBuffer structure containing buffer metadata\n  bFillValue - Byte value to fill the buffer with (typically 0 for clear)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Layout (SmackBuffer offsets used):\n  +0x10  dwRowWidth   Row width in bytes\n  +0x14  nHeight      Number of rows\n  +0x18  dwStride     Bytes per row (pitch)\n  +0x448 pBufferData  Pointer to pixel buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns immediately if pSmackBuf is NULL\n  - Returns immediately if height <= 0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x448 - Offset to buffer data pointer in SmackBuffer structure",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
