      "name": "SmackSetSystemRes",
      "signature": "bool SmackSetSystemRes(dword dwResolutionMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Sets the system display resolution for Smacker video playback.\n\nDynamically loads ChangeDisplaySettingsA from user32.dll on first call,\nthen uses it to change the display mode based on the resolution mode parameter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwResolutionMode is in range 0-4, return false if invalid\n2. If g_pfnChangeDisplaySettings is NULL, dynamically load it from user32.dll\n3. If loading failed (cached as -1), return false\n4. If mode 0: Reset to default display settings (pass NULL DEVMODE)\n5. If mode 1-4: Set up DEVMODE structure with resolution and call API\n6. Return true if ChangeDisplaySettingsA returns DISP_CHANGE_SUCCESSFUL (0)\n\nParameters:\n  dwResolutionMode - Display resolution mode selector:\n    0 = Reset to default (CDS_RESET)\n    1 = 640x400\n    2 = 640x480\n    3 = 800x600\n    4 = 1024x768\n\nReturns:\n  true  - Display mode change succeeded (DISP_CHANGE_SUCCESSFUL)\n  false - Invalid mode, API not available, or mode change failed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x9c (156)    - sizeof(DEVMODEA) structure\n  0x180000      - dmFields flags (DM_PELSWIDTH | DM_PELSHEIGHT)\n  4             - CDS_FULLSCREEN flag for ChangeDisplaySettingsA\n  0xffffffff    - Cached sentinel indicating API load failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - First call lazy-loads ChangeDisplaySettingsA via GetProcAddress\n  - API pointer cached at g_pfnChangeDisplaySettings (0x10014078)\n  - Returns false if user32.dll or API not found",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
