      "name": "_SmackDDSurfaceType@4",
      "signature": "uint _SmackDDSurfaceType@4(void * pDirectDrawSurface)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Determines the Smacker-compatible surface type from a DirectDraw surface's pixel format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize DDPIXELFORMAT structure with size (0x20) and flags (DDPF_RGB=0x40)\n2. Call IDirectDrawSurface::GetPixelFormat via vtable offset 0x54\n3. Check dwRGBBitCount for 8-bit palettized mode\n4. Check RGB bitmasks for 16-bit RGB565 format (R:0xF800, G:0x7E0, B:0x1F)\n5. Check RGB bitmasks for 16-bit RGB555 format (R:0x7C00, G:0x3E0, B:0x1F)\n6. Return unknown format code if no match\n\nParameters:\n  pDirectDrawSurface - Pointer to IDirectDrawSurface interface (COM object)\n\nReturns:\n  0x00000000 - 8-bit palettized surface (256 colors)\n  0xC0000000 - 16-bit RGB565 surface (65K colors, 5-6-5 bit layout)\n  0x80000000 - 16-bit RGB555 surface (32K colors, 5-5-5 bit layout)\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Unknown/unsupported pixel format\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x20 - sizeof(DDPIXELFORMAT)\n  0x40 - DDPF_RGB flag\n  0x54 - IDirectDrawSurface::GetPixelFormat vtable offset\n  0xF800 - RGB565 red mask (5 bits: 11111000 00000000)\n  0x7E0  - RGB565 green mask (6 bits: 00000111 11100000)\n  0x7C00 - RGB555 red mask (5 bits: 01111100 00000000)\n  0x3E0  - RGB555 green mask (5 bits: 00000011 11100000)\n  0x1F   - Blue mask for both 16-bit formats (5 bits: 00011111)\n\nStructure Layout (DDPIXELFORMAT on stack):\n  Offset  Size  Field             Value/Purpose\n  0x00    4     dwSize            0x20 (structure size)\n  0x04    4     dwFlags           0x40 (DDPF_RGB)\n  0x08    4     dwFourCC          (unused for RGB)\n  0x0C    4     dwRGBBitCount     8, 16, 24, or 32\n  0x10    4     dwRBitMask        Red channel bitmask\n  0x14    4     dwGBitMask        Green channel bitmask\n  0x18    4     dwBBitMask        Blue channel bitmask\n  0x1C    4     dwRGBAlphaBitMask Alpha channel bitmask",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
