      "name": "IsSoftwareCursor",
      "signature": "uint IsSoftwareCursor(int * pSmackBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Determines if the system requires software cursor rendering.\n\nTests whether the hardware cursor can be used by creating a temporary window,\nhiding the cursor, modifying a pixel in the SmackBuffer, and checking if the\ncursor drawing affected the pixel. Uses caching to avoid repeated expensive tests.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check GetSystemMetrics(SM_MOUSEPRESENT) - return 0 if no mouse\n2. Lock SmackBuffer using vtable Lock method (offset 0x64)\n3. Handle BUSY error (0x887601c2) by calling Wait (offset 0x6c)\n4. Check cached parameters against current cursor/buffer state\n5. If cache hit, return cached result immediately\n6. Register temporary window class and create 32x32 popup window at cursor\n7. Hide cursor completely using ShowCursor loop\n8. Get pixel at cursor position using GetDC/GetPixel\n9. Set test cursor and restore cursor visibility\n10. Lock buffer again, write test byte, unlock\n11. Compare pixel - if changed, hardware cursor works (return 1)\n12. If unchanged, restore pixel with SetPixel (return 0)\n13. Cleanup: DestroyWindow, UnregisterClass, restore cursor state\n14. Cache result in global g_dwSoftwareCursorResult\n\nParameters:\npSmackBuffer - Pointer to SmackBuffer with vtable for Lock/Unlock/Wait\n\nReturns:\n1 - Hardware cursor works (software cursor NOT needed)\n0 - Hardware cursor failed or no mouse present (software cursor needed)\n\nPhantom Variables:\nauStack_a4 - Assembly-only MSG structure for PeekMessageA, not in decompiled code",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
