      "name": "_SmackCheckCursor@20",
      "signature": "int _SmackCheckCursor@20(HWND hWnd, int nClientX, int nClientY, int nWidth, int nHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Checks if the system cursor overlaps a specified rectangular region and hides it if so.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize cursor width/height from system metrics if not cached\n2. Convert client coordinates to screen coordinates if window handle provided\n3. Get current cursor position\n4. Check if cursor bounding box overlaps the specified rectangle\n5. If overlapping, repeatedly call ShowCursor(FALSE) until display count goes negative\n\nParameters:\n  hWnd - Window handle for coordinate conversion (NULL for screen coordinates)\n  nClientX - Left edge of region in client/screen coordinates\n  nClientY - Top edge of region in client/screen coordinates  \n  nWidth - Width of the region to check\n  nHeight - Height of the region to check\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of times ShowCursor(FALSE) was called to hide the cursor (0 if not hidden)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If hWnd is NULL, nClientX/nClientY are treated as screen coordinates\n  - Cursor dimensions cached in g_nCursorWidth/g_nCursorHeight after first call\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x0D (13) - SM_CXCURSOR: System cursor width\n  0x0E (14) - SM_CYCURSOR: System cursor height",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:be1b876ba5b61512ac7cdc9e54fd8d075127912b85ee90099afb9414601e76a0",
