      "name": "SmackReadFrame",
      "signature": "int SmackReadFrame(void * pSmack)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Reads next frame data from Smacker video file with frame rate synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if stream position at offset 0x374 + 0x3c (0x3b0) has reached end marker\n  2. If at end, return error (data already read)\n  3. Capture start time using timeGetTime() -> dwStartTick\n  4. Read frame data from file using ReadFile with parameters:\n     - File handle from offset 0xc\n     - Buffer pointer from offset 0x374\n     - Bytes to read from offset 0x3b0\n     - Output bytes read to local dwBytesRead\n  5. Update stream position: offset 0x374 += dwBytesRead\n  6. Update bytes remaining: offset 0x3b0 -= dwBytesRead\n  7. Check if more data to read (offset 0x3b0 > 0)\n  8. Calculate frame delay based on frame rate:\n     - Read frame rate from offset 0x1000\n     - Compute delay = (qwNumerator * 0x3e8 (1000)) / qwDenominator\n  9. Busy-wait loop using timeGetTime() until delay elapsed\n 10. Return success status\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack  - Pointer to SmackContext structure containing:\n            - File handle (offset 0xc)\n            - Buffer pointer (offset 0x374)\n            - Bytes remaining (offset 0x3b0)\n            - Stream position marker (offset 0x3c)\n            - Frame rate data (offset 0x1000)\n\nReturns:\n  Non-zero on success (frame read and timing synchronized)\n  Zero on failure (end of data or read error)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if stream position already at end marker\n  - Frame rate timing uses multimedia timer (timeGetTime) for synchronization\n  - Delay calculation: milliseconds = (numerator * 1000) / denominator\n\nSmackContext Structure Layout (partial):\n  Offset | Size | Field            | Type   | Description\n  -------|------|------------------|--------|----------------------------------\n  0x000c |    4 | hFile            | HANDLE | File handle for video data\n  0x003c |    4 | dwEndMarker      | DWORD  | End of stream position marker\n  0x0374 |    4 | pBufferCurrent   | void*  | Current read buffer pointer\n  0x03b0 |    4 | cbBytesRemaining | DWORD  | Bytes remaining to read\n  0x1000 |    ? | frameRateData    | ?      | Frame rate timing structure",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
