      "name": "ReadFileWithBuffer",
      "signature": "uint ReadFileWithBuffer(int pSmack, byte * pBuffer, uint dwBytesToRead)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Reads bytes from a file with optional ring buffer support and rate throttling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Record start time using timeGetTime() for rate limiting calculations\n  2. Check if buffering is disabled (pSmack+0x450 == 0):\n     a. If disabled: perform single ReadFile() call directly to output buffer\n     b. If enabled: proceed to buffered read algorithm (step 3)\n  3. Buffered read loop (until all bytes read or error):\n     a. Copy available bytes from ring buffer (pSmack+0x460) to output\n     b. Update buffer pointers (pSmack+0x458) and wrap at end (pSmack+0x454)\n     c. If more bytes needed and buffer empty: refill via ReadFile()\n     d. For large reads (>0x1000): bypass buffer, read in 0x4000 (16KB) chunks\n     e. Call progress callback if registered (g_pfnProgressCallback)\n  4. Rate throttling (if pSmack+0x4c4 != 0):\n     a. Calculate target time: dwStartTime + (dwBytesReturned * 1000) / dwThrottleRate\n     b. Spin-wait on timeGetTime() until target time reached\n  5. Update cumulative byte counter (pSmack+0x46c)\n  6. Update cumulative elapsed time (pSmack+0x470)\n  7. Return total bytes successfully read\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack        - Pointer to Smack file handle structure containing file handle,\n                  ring buffer state, and throttling configuration\n  pBuffer       - Destination buffer to receive read data\n  dwBytesToRead - Number of bytes requested to read\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Number of bytes successfully read and placed in pBuffer\n         May be less than requested if EOF reached or read error occurs\n         Returns 0 on immediate failure or when nothing available\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Direct mode (pSmack+0x450 == 0): single ReadFile, no buffering overhead\n  - Ring buffer wrap: when pbBufferCurrent reaches pbBufferEnd, resets to pbBufferStart\n  - Large reads (>4KB): bypass ring buffer, read directly in 16KB aligned chunks\n  - Rate limiting: spin-waits to maintain target throughput in bytes/second\n  - EOF/Error: sets pSmack+0x3a8 = 1 on short read (fewer bytes than requested)\n\nSmack Structure Layout (relevant fields):\nOffset | Size | Field             | Type   | Description\n-------|------|-------------------|--------|------------------------------------------\n0x3a8  |  4   | dwErrorFlags      | DWORD  | Error/status flags (bit 0 = EOF/error)\n0x3b0  |  4   | hFile             | HANDLE | Windows file handle for ReadFile\n0x450  |  4   | pbBufferStart     | DWORD  | Ring buffer base (0 = direct mode)\n0x454  |  4   | pbBufferEnd       | DWORD  | Ring buffer end boundary\n0x458  |  4   | pbBufferCurrent   | DWORD  | Current read position in buffer\n0x45c  |  4   | pbBufferReset     | DWORD  | Reset position for refill\n0x460  |  4   | cbBufferAvailable | DWORD  | Bytes available in buffer\n0x464  |  4   | cbBufferWrap      | DWORD  | Wrap size calculation\n0x468  |  4   | dwTotalRead       | DWORD  | Statistics: total bytes read\n0x46c  |  4   | dwCumulativeBytes | DWORD  | Cumulative byte counter\n0x470  |  4   | dwElapsedTime     | DWORD  | Cumulative elapsed time (ms)\n0x4c4  |  4   | dwThrottleRate    | DWORD  | Target bytes/sec (0 = no limit)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
