      "name": "_SmackSoundOnOff@8",
      "signature": "int _SmackSoundOnOff@8(int nSmack, int nOnOffFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Controls sound playback state for Smacker video audio tracks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pSmack pointer - return 0 if NULL\n2. Check if sound is initialized (offset 0x444 != -1) - return 1 if uninitialized\n3. If dwOnOffFlags is non-zero (turn ON):\n   a. If sound already on, iterate through 7 audio channels\n   b. Lock each channel buffer via DirectSound\n   c. Calculate silence fill pattern (0x00 or 0x80 based on format)\n   d. Fill unused buffer regions with silence pattern using REP STOSD/STOSB\n   e. Update track position and byte counters\n   f. Call user callback g_pfnSoundOnCallback if set\n   g. Release DirectSound buffer locks\n   h. Clear sound-on flag when complete\n4. If dwOnOffFlags is zero (turn OFF):\n   a. Store current frame position for later resume\n   b. Set sound-on flag to 1\n   c. Reset all 7 channel track states\n   d. For each active track, call user notify callback and reset positions\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack - Pointer to Smack structure containing video/audio state\n  dwOnOffFlags - Non-zero to turn sound ON, zero to turn sound OFF\n                 Bit 31 (0x80000000) affects buffer fill behavior\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Failure (NULL pSmack pointer)\n  1 - Success (sound state changed or already in requested state)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x444 - Smack structure sound initialized flag offset\n  0x44c - Smack structure sound-on state flag offset\n  0x374 - Current frame position offset\n  0x50c - Saved frame position offset\n  0x428 - Start of channel pointer array (7 channels, 4 bytes each)\n  0x80  - 8-bit PCM silence value (128)\n  0x00  - 16-bit PCM silence value (0)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
