      "name": "_SmackClose@4",
      "signature": "void _SmackClose@4(undefined4 * pSmack)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Closes and deallocates a Smack video/audio handle and all associated resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate handle is not null - return immediately if null\n2. If debug mode enabled (g_bDebugAudio == 1), output handle address to debug console via OutputDebugStringA\n3. If audio tracks are initialized (pSmack->dwAudioInitFlag != -1):\n   a. Iterate through 7 audio track buffer slots at offsets 0x428-0x440\n   b. For each non-null slot: unlink from callback list via g_pfnUnlinkListNodeCallback\n   c. Free nested buffer pointed to by track buffer via SmackFree\n   d. Free the audio track buffer itself via SmackFree\n   e. Decrement global audio buffer reference count (g_dwProgressCallbackCount)\n   f. Mark audio tracks as uninitialized (set dwAudioInitFlag to -1)\n4. If global reference count reaches 0 and shared buffer exists, free g_pSmackAudioBuffer\n5. Close file handle via CloseHandle if valid (!= -1) and not externally managed (SMACK_FILEHANDLE flag not set)\n6. Free individual buffers if non-null: pFrameBuffer2, pFrameBuffer1, pPaletteBuffer, pHuffmanTables, pExtraBuffer\n7. Save dwFlags before zeroing structure\n8. Zero entire handle structure using REP STOSD (0x144 dwords = 0x510 bytes)\n9. Free handle memory via SmackFree unless SMACK_DONT_FREE_HANDLE flag (0x2000000) is set\n\nParameters:\npSmack - Pointer to Smack handle structure to close (Smack*)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null handle check prevents null pointer dereference\n- SMACK_FILEHANDLE flag (0x1000 in dwFlags) prevents closing externally provided file handles\n- SMACK_DONT_FREE_HANDLE flag (0x2000000 in dwFlags) prevents freeing the handle itself\n\nStructure Layout (Smack Handle - key fields):\nOffset   Size  Field              Description\n0x390    4     dwFlags            Handle flags (SMACK_FILEHANDLE, SMACK_DONT_FREE_HANDLE, etc.)\n0x3B0    4     hFile              File handle for Smack file (-1 if invalid)\n0x3B8    4     pFrameBuffer1      First frame buffer pointer\n0x3BC    4     pFrameBuffer2      Second frame buffer pointer\n0x3D0    4     pHuffmanTables     Huffman decompression tables\n0x3E0    4     pPaletteBuffer     Palette data buffer\n0x428    28    apAudioTrackBufs   Array of 7 audio track buffer pointers (4 bytes each)\n0x444    4     dwAudioInitFlag    Audio initialization state (-1 = not initialized)\n0x450    4     pExtraBuffer       Additional buffer pointer",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
