      "name": "ProcessSmackFrame",
      "signature": "uint ProcessSmackFrame(int pSmack)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Processes a single Smacker video frame with audio synchronization and palette conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pSmack pointer, return 0 if null\n2. Check if frame is already being processed (offset 0x3a8), return 0 if busy\n3. Get current time via timeGetTime() and initialize timing fields\n4. If first frame, store initial timestamp at offset 0x490\n5. If audio enabled (offset 0x68), copy audio buffer pointer\n6. Increment frame counter at offset 0x49c\n7. Process audio tracks via ProcessSmackAudioTracks()\n8. If sound buffer active (offset 0x424):\n   - Check buffer readiness via CheckSoundBufferReady()\n   - If SMACK_NOSYNC flag (0x400) not set, compute skip decision\n9. If frame data pointer valid (offset 0x3bc) and not skipping:\n   - Set frame active flag at offset 0x408\n   - If palette destination valid (offset 0x3c8):\n     - Convert palette based on format byte:\n       - 0x80 (-128): RGB24 to RGB555\n       - 0xC0 (-64): RGB24 to RGB565\n     - Copy 512 bytes (128 DWORDs) of palette to global buffer\n   - Decode frame via DecodeSmackerFrame()\n10. If skipping frame, increment skip counter at offset 0x4a0\n11. Invoke progress callback if registered\n12. Return sound buffer status\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack - Pointer to Smack structure containing video/audio state\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Sound buffer status (0 = not ready or error, non-zero = ready)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x80 (cPaletteFormat) - RGB555 palette format identifier\n  0xC0 (cPaletteFormat) - RGB565 palette format identifier\n  0x400 (flags) - SMACK_NOSYNC flag, disables audio sync wait\n  0x80 (loop) - 128 DWORDs = 512 bytes palette size\n\nStructure Offsets (Smack):\n  Offset   | Size | Description\n  0x68     | 4    | Audio buffer pointer (non-zero if audio enabled)\n  0x6c     | var  | RGB24 palette source data\n  0x374    | 4    | Audio buffer copy source\n  0x390    | 4    | Flags field (bit 10 = NOSYNC)\n  0x3a8    | 4    | Busy/processing flag\n  0x3b8    | 4    | Decoder source buffer\n  0x3bc    | 4    | Frame data pointer\n  0x3c4    | 4    | Palette conversion enabled flag\n  0x3c8    | 4    | Palette destination pointer\n  0x3d8    | 4    | Audio buffer copy destination\n  0x404    | 4    | Decoder destination buffer\n  0x408    | 4    | Frame active flag (set to 1 during decode)\n  0x424    | 4    | Sound buffer handle (non-zero if active)\n  0x484    | 4    | Last frame timestamp\n  0x488    | 4    | Current frame timestamp\n  0x490    | 4    | First frame timestamp (initialized once)\n  0x49c    | 4    | Frame counter\n  0x4a0    | 4    | Skipped frame counter",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b381a0ba492da7373a85975ee1ee83375f6d72f6dcc81539c3d902e9859507be",
