      "name": "AccumulateFrameTimingStats",
      "signature": "void AccumulateFrameTimingStats(int pSmk)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Accumulates frame timing statistics for Smack video playback profiling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. If frame timing started (offset 0x484 != 0):\n     a. Get current time via timeGetTime()\n     b. Calculate elapsed frame time = currentTime - frameStartTime\n     c. Clear frame start timestamp (0x484 = 0)\n     d. Update slowest frame tracking:\n        - If elapsed > slowest time (0x4ac): shift slowest to second, record new slowest\n        - Else if elapsed > second slowest (0x4b0): update second slowest\n  2. If decompress timing started (offset 0x48c != 0):\n     a. Get current time (reuse if already fetched)\n     b. Add elapsed time to decompress accumulator (0x4a4)\n     c. Clear decompress start timestamp\n  3. If blit timing started (offset 0x488 != 0):\n     a. Get current time (reuse if already fetched)\n     b. Add elapsed time to blit accumulator (0x4a8)\n     c. Clear blit start timestamp\n\nParameters:\n  pSmk - Pointer to Smack video structure containing timing fields\n\nReturns:\n  void - Updates timing statistics in-place within Smack structure\n\nStructure Offsets (relative to pSmk):\n  Offset | Size | Field                  | Description\n  -------|------|------------------------|----------------------------------\n  0x374  | 4    | dwCurrentFrame         | Current frame number\n  0x484  | 4    | dwFrameStartTime       | Frame start timestamp (ms)\n  0x488  | 4    | dwBlitStartTime        | Blit start timestamp (ms)\n  0x48c  | 4    | dwDecompressStartTime  | Decompress start timestamp (ms)\n  0x4a4  | 4    | dwTotalDecompressTime  | Accumulated decompress time (ms)\n  0x4a8  | 4    | dwTotalBlitTime        | Accumulated blit time (ms)\n  0x4ac  | 4    | dwSlowestFrameTime     | Slowest frame elapsed time (ms)\n  0x4b0  | 4    | dwSecondSlowestTime    | Second slowest frame time (ms)\n  0x4b4  | 4    | dwSlowestFrameNum      | Frame number of slowest frame\n  0x4b8  | 4    | dwSecondSlowestNum     | Frame number of second slowest",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
