      "name": "_SmackNextFrame@4",
      "signature": "void _SmackNextFrame@4(int pSmk)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Advances a Smack video to the next frame.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return early if pSmk is NULL\n2. If video is paused (offset 0x3a8 != 0), increment frame counter and return\n3. Call progress callback if registered (g_pfnSmackSoundInit)\n4. Accumulate timing statistics for the current frame\n5. Read frame size from frame size table at offset 0x3dc indexed by current frame\n6. Increment frame index at offset 0x374\n7. Add frame size to cumulative data offset at 0x3d4\n8. If more frames remain (frame index < total frames at offset 0xc), read next frame data\n9. Decompress the current frame\n10. Call progress callback again if registered\n\nParameters:\n  pSmk - Smack * - Pointer to Smack video structure\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pSmk returns immediately without processing\n  - Paused state (offset 0x3a8 != 0) only increments frame counter\n\nStructure Offsets:\n  Offset   Size  Field              Description\n  0x00c    4     dwFrameCount       Total number of frames in video\n  0x374    4     dwCurrentFrame     Current frame index (0-based)\n  0x3a8    4     dwPauseFlag        Non-zero when video is paused\n  0x3d4    4     dwDataOffset       Cumulative byte offset into video data\n  0x3dc    4     pFrameSizeTable    Pointer to array of frame sizes (uint[dwFrameCount])",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:0f24c5ad421889fd31b70e36688208ce27dc4d1ba231796c2be2476779182e7d",
