      "name": "RenderSmackFrameToScreen",
      "signature": "void RenderSmackFrameToScreen(int pSmack, dword dwSrcPitch, int nSrcYOffset, int nDestWidth, int nPaletteTable, int nPaletteOffset, dword dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Renders a Smack video frame to the screen with scaling and palette support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pSmack is non-null; return early if null\n2. Handle 320-width (0x140) special case: force palette base 0xa0000, offset 0\n3. If previous blit context exists at pSmack+0x3bc:\n   a. Preserve palette data pointer from pSmack+0x3c8\n   b. If context type==1, save stride and buffer data pointer\n   c. Adjust allocation tracking at pSmack+0x480\n4. Extract scale mode flags from pSmack+0x390:\n   - 0x100000: Double width mode (width*2, height/2)\n   - 0x200000: Interlaced mode (width*2, height/2, 8x multiplier)\n5. Calculate display list buffer size based on frame dimensions and scale\n6. Allocate display list buffer via FUN_10004c80\n7. Initialize display list header:\n   - Byte 0: Type marker (0)\n   - Byte 1: Interlace flag\n   - Byte 2: Alpha/transparency value from dwFlags high byte\n8. Copy palette data (0x200 bytes) if previous palette exists\n9. Build display list entries via FUN_10006a90:\n   - Handle 64KB segment boundary crossings\n   - Generate bank switch commands (0xfffe, 0xfffd, 0xffff)\n   - Track palette indices per segment\n10. Terminate display list with 0xffff marker\n11. Clean up previous context via ApplyPresetUnitTileAttributes\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack: Pointer to Smack video structure containing frame data\n  dwSrcPitch: Source pitch (bytes per row), aligned to 4-byte boundary\n  nSrcYOffset: Y offset into source frame for partial blits\n  nDestWidth: Destination width (320=0x140 triggers special mode)\n  nPaletteTable: Base address of palette lookup table\n  nPaletteOffset: Offset into palette table\n  dwFlags: Bit flags controlling rendering:\n    - Bits 30-31 (0xc0000000): Palette mode selector\n    - Bits 24-29: Alpha/transparency value\n\nReturns: void (modifies Smack structure in place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - 320-width mode: Forces VGA palette base (0xa0000), clears offset\n  - Null pSmack: Early return with no operation\n  - 64KB boundary: Generates bank switch display commands\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x140 (320): Standard VGA width, triggers compatibility mode\n  0xa0000: VGA video memory base address\n  0x3bc: Offset to blit context pointer in Smack structure\n  0x3c8: Offset to palette data pointer in Smack structure\n  0x390: Offset to render flags in Smack structure\n  0x100000: Double-width scaling flag\n  0x200000: Interlaced rendering flag\n  0x200: Palette data size (512 bytes)\n  0x400: Palette table offset in display list\n  0x600: Base header size for display list\n  0xfffe: Bank switch command (continue next segment)\n  0xfffd: Interlace sync command\n  0xffff: End of display list marker",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
