      "name": "_SmackToBuffer@28",
      "signature": "void _SmackToBuffer@28(int pSmack, uint dwLeftOffset, uint dwTopOffset, uint dwPitch, uint dwDestHeight, byte * pDestBuffer, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Configures and initializes the Smacker video playback buffer for rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pSmack pointer, early exit if NULL\n2. If pDestBuffer is NULL (cleanup mode):\n   a. Free existing buffer via ApplyPresetUnitTileAttributes\n   b. Update memory tracking and clear buffer pointer\n   c. Return early\n3. Calculate adjusted dimensions based on scaling flags:\n   - 0x100000: Horizontal scaling (halve height, double pitch)\n   - 0x200000: Vertical scaling (set pixel mode to 7, halve height)\n4. Determine bytes per pixel (1 or 2) based on dwFlags high bits\n5. Calculate required buffer size via CalcSmackerBufferOffset\n6. Allocate or reuse existing buffer:\n   - If buffer exists but is too small, free it first\n   - Allocate new buffer via FUN_10004c80\n   - Zero-initialize the new buffer\n7. Set up palette transfer area if scaling enabled (512 bytes at buffer end)\n8. Copy previous palette data if it exists\n9. Configure SmackBuffer header structure:\n   - Offset +0x00: Valid flag (1)\n   - Offset +0x01: Vertical scale flag\n   - Offset +0x02: Scale factor from dwFlags high byte\n   - Offset +0x04: Destination pointer calculation\n   - Offset +0x08: Width in DWORDs\n   - Offset +0x0C: Height in DWORDs\n   - Offset +0x10-0x1C: Row stride calculations (depends on flip flag)\n   - Offset +0x24: Frame width\n   - Offset +0x28: Adjusted height\n10. Free old buffer if it was replaced\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack (Smack *): Pointer to Smacker video handle structure\n  dwLeftOffset (uint): Horizontal offset in destination buffer (pixels)\n  dwTopOffset (uint): Vertical offset in destination buffer (pixels)\n  dwPitch (uint): Destination buffer stride in bytes\n  dwDestHeight (uint): Total height of destination buffer\n  pDestBuffer (byte *): Destination surface pointer, or NULL to free buffer\n  dwFlags (uint): Rendering flags:\n    - Bit 0 (0x01): Flip vertically\n    - Bits 30-31: Scale mode (0=no extra palette, else reserve 512 bytes)\n    - Bits 24-31: Scale factor value\n\nReturns:\n  void - Buffer configuration stored in Smack structure at offsets:\n    +0x3BC: Pointer to SmackBuffer\n    +0x3C0: Buffer size\n    +0x3C8: Palette area pointer\n    +0x394: Left offset cache\n    +0x398: Top offset cache\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pSmack: Returns immediately\n  - NULL pDestBuffer: Cleanup mode, frees existing buffer\n  - Existing buffer too small: Reallocates\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x3BC - SmackBuffer pointer offset in Smack structure\n  0x3C0 - Buffer size offset\n  0x3C8 - Palette pointer offset\n  0x390 - Flags offset (scaling modes)\n  0x394 - Cached left offset\n  0x398 - Cached top offset\n  0x480 - Memory tracking offset\n  0x100000 - Horizontal scaling flag\n  0x200000 - Vertical scaling flag\n  0xC0000000 - Scale mode mask\n  0x200 - Palette buffer size (512 bytes)\n  0x80 - Palette DWORD count (128 entries)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
