      "name": "_SmackColorTrans@8",
      "signature": "void _SmackColorTrans@8(int pSmack, byte * pbPalette)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Applies color translation/palette remapping to a Smack video handle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pSmack pointer is non-null\n2. If progress callback is registered, invoke it (pre-operation notification)\n3. Extract internal Smack structure from offset 0x3B8 of the handle\n4. Call SmackRemapFramePalettes to apply palette translation\n5. If progress callback is registered, invoke it (post-operation notification)\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack    - Pointer to Smack video handle containing video state\n  pbPalette - Pointer to 256-entry palette array (768 bytes RGB or 1024 bytes RGBA)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pSmack is NULL, function returns immediately without any processing\n  - Progress callbacks at g_pfnSmackSoundInit are invoked before and after remapping\n    if g_dwProgressCallbackCount is non-zero\n\nStructure Access:\n  Offset    Size  Field                 Description\n  0x3B8     4     pInternalSmack        Pointer to internal Smack structure for remapping",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:6c163796a67c7b119589e7414b1c56e44fa550754259ce790a9287729ced9944",
