      "name": "_SmackColorRemap@16",
      "signature": "void _SmackColorRemap@16(int nSmackHandle, uint dwPalette, uint dwPaletteSize, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Creates a color remap table by finding closest matching colors between source and destination palettes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if pSmackHandle is NULL (video handle required)\n2. Call optional callback function at [0x10015e88] if [0x10014298] is set (pre-remap hook)\n3. Clamp dwPaletteSize to maximum of 256 entries\n4. Initialize channel offsets based on dwFlags:\n   - Bit 2 (0x4): BGR byte order instead of RGB\n   - Bit 3 (0x8): Combine with bit 2 for alternate component ordering\n   - Bit 1 (0x2): Swap red/green channel offsets\n   - Bit 0 (0x1): Double all offsets (16-bit color mode)\n5. For each of 256 palette indices:\n   a. Extract source RGB components from internal palette at [pSmackHandle+0x6c]\n   b. For each entry in destination palette (pbPalette):\n      - Calculate squared difference for each RGB channel\n      - Sum squared differences for total color distance\n      - Track minimum distance and best matching index\n   c. Store best match index in remap table (256-byte array at ESP+0x54)\n6. Call SmackRemapFramePalettes(pSmackHandle+0x3b8, remapTable) to apply remap\n\nParameters:\npSmackHandle - Pointer to Smack video handle structure containing internal palette at offset 0x6c\n               and frame palette pointer at offset 0x3b8\npbPalette    - Pointer to source palette data (RGB triplets, byte array)\ndwPaletteSize - Number of palette entries to process (clamped to 256 max)\ndwFlags      - Color format flags controlling channel order and bit depth\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; updates internal remap table via SmackRemapFramePalettes\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x100 (256) - Maximum palette entries\n0x6c  (108) - Offset to internal palette in Smack handle\n0x3b8 (952) - Offset to frame palette pointer in Smack handle\n0x4, 0x8, 0x2, 0x1 - Flag bits for color format configuration",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
