      "name": "_SmackGetTrackData@12",
      "signature": "uint _SmackGetTrackData@12(int pSmack, uint * pDestBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Retrieves audio track data from the current Smack video frame.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Validate pSmack pointer is non-null\\n2. Check if Smack structure is in valid state (offset 0x3a8 must be 0)\\n3. Call FindFirstSetBitAndClear on track request flags to get track index\\n4. Validate track index is in range 0-6 (Smacker supports up to 7 audio tracks)\\n5. Get track data pointer from track array at pSmack+0x3e8 (offset 1000)\\n6. Check track flags at pSmack+0x48+(trackIndex*4) for compression bit 0x80000000\\n7. If compressed (bit set):\\n   a. Allocate 0x2000 byte audio buffer if g_pSmackAudioBuffer is null\\n   b. Call DecompressSmackFrame to decompress audio to destination\\n   c. Return compressed size from trackData[1]\\n8. If uncompressed (bit clear):\\n   a. Get data size from trackData[0]\\n   b. Skip if size is 3 or 4 (header only, no payload)\\n   c. Copy (size-4) bytes from trackData+4 to destination buffer\\n   d. Return (size-4) as bytes copied\\n\\nParameters:\\n  pSmack      - Pointer to Smack video structure handle\\n  pDestBuffer - Pointer to destination buffer for audio data output\\n\\nReturns:\\n  uint - Number of bytes written to pDestBuffer on success\\n  0    - On failure (null handle, invalid state, invalid track, alloc failure)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  Returns 0 if pSmack is null\\n  Returns 0 if Smack state at offset 0x3a8 is non-zero (busy/invalid)\\n  Returns 0 if track index exceeds 6\\n  Returns 0 if track data pointer is null\\n  Returns 0 if audio buffer allocation fails\\n\\nMagic Numbers:\\n  0x3a8 - Smack state/lock flag offset\\n  0x3e8 (1000) - Track data pointer array offset\\n  0x48 - Track flags array offset\\n  0x80000000 - Compression flag bit in track flags\\n  0x2000 - Audio decompression buffer size (8KB)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
