      "name": "_SmackToBufferRect@8",
      "signature": "int _SmackToBufferRect@8(int nUnused1, int nUnused2, int pSmk, int nFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Retrieves the next dirty rectangle from the Smack video frame's update queue.\n\nThis function is part of the Smacker video codec's dirty rectangle tracking system.\nIt processes the queue of screen regions that have changed during video decoding and\nreturns coordinate information for the next rectangle to be redrawn.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pSmk pointer - return 0 if null\n2. Initialize timing if first call (timestamp at offset 0x48c)\n3. Update elapsed time tracking (offsets 0x488, 0x4a8)\n4. Check if buffer update mode is active (offset 0x408)\n5. If active and nFlags != 2, process dirty rect queue:\n   - Call ComputeSmackBufferRect to validate rectangles\n   - Remove invalid entries via RemoveArrayElementCompact\n   - Continue until queue count less than 16 or no more removals\n6. Return 0 if queue is empty\n7. Pop next rectangle from queue (decrement count at 0x4c8)\n8. Copy rectangle coordinates to output fields:\n   - Offset 0x380: Left (X)\n   - Offset 0x384: Top (Y)\n   - Offset 0x388: Width\n   - Offset 0x38c: Height\n9. Shift remaining queue entries forward (memcpy via MOVSD)\n10. Return 1 to indicate rectangle was retrieved\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused1 (ECX): Unused fastcall register parameter\n  nUnused2 (EDX): Unused fastcall register parameter  \n  pSmk: Pointer to Smack video structure\n  nFlags: Rendering flags (2 = skip processing)\n\nReturns:\n  1: Rectangle coordinates copied to pSmk output fields\n  0: No rectangles available or invalid state\n\nSSA Variables (compiler-generated, cannot be renamed):\n  DVar1 (dwTimestamp): Return value from timeGetTime()\n  iVar2 (nPrevTime/nComputeResult): Previous timestamp or rect validation result\n  uVar3 (dwQueueIndex/dwCopyCount): Queue byte offset or copy loop counter\n  pcbArraySize (pdwRectCount): Pointer to queue count at Smk+0x4c8\n  puVar4 (pdwSrc): Source pointer for queue shift copy\n  puVar5 (pdwDst): Destination pointer for queue shift copy\n  extraout_ECX/EDX: Clobbered register values after function calls\n\nStructure Layout (Smack offsets used):\n  Offset   Size  Field              Description\n  0x380    4     nOutLeft           Output: rectangle left X\n  0x384    4     nOutTop            Output: rectangle top Y\n  0x388    4     nOutWidth          Output: rectangle width\n  0x38c    4     nOutHeight         Output: rectangle height\n  0x408    4     bBufferActive      Buffer update mode flag\n  0x488    4     dwPrevTimestamp    Previous timing value\n  0x48c    4     dwTimestamp        Current timing (timeGetTime)\n  0x4a8    4     dwElapsedAccum     Accumulated elapsed time\n  0x4c8    4     nRectQueueCount    Number of rects in queue (x4)\n  0x4cc    64    aRectQueue[16]     Rectangle queue array (4 dwords each)\n  0x4dc    ...   ...                Extended queue storage",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
