      "name": "ComputeSmackBufferRect",
      "signature": "int ComputeSmackBufferRect(dword dwUnused1, dword dwUnused2, dword pSmackCtx, int nMode, dword * pOutputRect)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Computes the output rectangle bounds for Smack video buffer rendering.\n\nThis function implements a state machine that processes Smack video blocks\nand calculates the visible dirty rectangle for partial screen updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check state at offset 0x408 in context structure\n2. If state == 3: Reset state to 0 and return 0 (done)\n3. If state == 1: Call SmackDecompressNextBlock to decode first block\n4. If decompress fails with no data at offset 0x68: return 0\n5. Otherwise transition state to 2 and continue processing\n6. State 2: Accumulate block bounds across multiple decompress calls\n7. Mode 0: Calculate rect size and clamp to available buffer\n8. Mode 1: Simple accumulation loop until decompress complete\n9. Apply 8-byte alignment to X coordinates for SIMD optimization\n10. Write final rect (x1, y1, x2, y2) to output array\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnused1 (ECX) - Unused register parameter (preserved for calling convention)\n  dwUnused2 (EDX) - Unused register parameter (preserved for calling convention)\n  pSmackCtx       - Pointer to Smack context structure containing video state\n  nMode           - Processing mode: 0 = size-limited, 1 = full accumulation\n  pOutputRect     - Output array of 4 dwords [x1, y1, x2, y2] for dirty rect\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Success, pOutputRect contains valid dirty rectangle\n  0 - No data to process or end of frame reached\n\nStructure Offsets in pSmackCtx:\n  +0x004: Video width limit\n  +0x068: Frame data available flag\n  +0x390: Video flags (bit 0x300000 = double resolution)\n  +0x394: X offset base\n  +0x398: Y offset base\n  +0x3BC: Decompressor context pointer\n  +0x408: State machine (0=init, 1=first, 2=processing, 3=done)\n  +0x40C: Current block X position\n  +0x410: Current block Y position  \n  +0x414: Block width\n  +0x418: Block height",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
