      "name": "RemoveArrayElementCompact",
      "signature": "void RemoveArrayElementCompact(int * pArray, uint dwMatchIndex, uint * pcbArraySize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Removes an element from a compact array by finding matching field patterns and shifting remaining elements.\n\nThis function searches the array for elements that share field values with the element at dwMatchIndex.\nWhen a match is found based on specific field comparison patterns, it copies the differing field value\nfrom the matched element to the current element, then compacts the array by removing the matched element.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop index to 0, scan from beginning of array\n2. Skip comparison if current index equals match index\n3. Compare current element against match element using two field patterns:\n   - Pattern 1: field0 and field2 match, then check field1/field3 cross-match\n   - Pattern 2: field1 and field3 match, then check field0/field2 cross-match\n4. On match found, copy the differing field value from match to current element\n5. Shift all elements after dwMatchIndex left by one position using REP MOVSD\n6. Decrement array size by 4 (one element worth of indices)\n7. Restart scan from beginning with updated array\n\nParameters:\n    pArray       - Pointer to CompactArrayElement array to modify\n    dwMatchIndex - Index (in dwords, not elements) of target element to remove\n    pcbArraySize - Pointer to array size counter (in dwords); decremented on removal\n\nReturns:\n    void - Array is modified in place; *pcbArraySize updated to reflect new size\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - Empty array (size=0): Returns immediately without modification\n    - No match found: Returns after full scan without modification\n    - Match at current index: Skipped to avoid self-comparison\n\nStructure Layout (CompactArrayElement, 16 bytes):\n    Offset  Size  Field   Type    Description\n    0x00    4     field0  dword   First comparison field\n    0x04    4     field1  dword   Second comparison field\n    0x08    4     field2  dword   Third comparison field\n    0x0C    4     field3  dword   Fourth comparison field\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x10 (16)     - Element stride in bytes (4 dwords per element)\n    0x04          - Index increment per element (dword-based indexing)\n    0x3FFFFFFF    - Mask for shift count calculation (30-bit limit)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
