      "name": "_SmackSoundInTrack@8",
      "signature": "int _SmackSoundInTrack@8(int pSmack, dword dwTrackMask)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Checks if a Smack video has valid audio data in any of the specified tracks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return 0 if pSmack is NULL\n2. Loop through set bits in dwTrackMask (bits 13-19 represent tracks 0-6)\n3. For each track, call FindFirstSetBitAndClear to get track index\n4. Read track audio flags from pSmack->TrackFlags[trackIndex] at offset 0x48\n5. Check if track has valid audio: bit 30 set AND lower 24 bits non-zero\n6. Return 1 if valid track found, continue loop otherwise\n7. Return 0 if no valid tracks remain in mask\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack (Smack*) - Pointer to Smack video structure\n  dwTrackMask (dword) - Bitmask of tracks to check (bits 13-19 = tracks 0-6)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Valid audio data found in at least one specified track\n  0 - No valid audio in any specified track, or pSmack is NULL\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xfe000 - Track bitmask (bits 13-19, 7 possible audio tracks)\n  0x48 - Offset to TrackFlags array in Smack structure\n  0x40000000 - Bit 30: Track has audio data flag\n  0x00ffffff - Lower 24 bits: Audio data size/presence indicator\n\nSSA Variables (compiler temporaries, cannot be renamed):\n  uVar1 - dwTrackFlags: Audio flags for current track from Smack structure\n  bVar2 - bTrackIndex: Track index (0-6) from FindFirstSetBitAndClear",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:0e3719b7e77cdff708c9e78ca2c0e0024ed59717c35a04a344808473a1a1264d",
