      "name": "_SmackWait@4",
      "signature": "int _SmackWait@4(int pSmk)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Waits for the appropriate time to display the next Smacker video frame.\n\nThis function implements frame timing synchronization for Smacker video playback.\nIt checks whether the current time has reached the next scheduled frame time,\nand if audio is active, synchronizes with audio buffer position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return 0 if handle is NULL or video is stopped (offset +0x3a8)\n2. Invoke sound progress callback if registered\n3. If audio track is inactive (index == -1):\n   a. Check frame ready flag at +0x41c\n   b. Get current time from timeGetTime() and scale by 100\n   c. If next frame time uninitialized (-1), set to current + interval\n   d. If current time >= next frame time, advance timing and set ready flag\n4. If audio track is active:\n   a. Check audio is playing (+0x448) and not paused (+0x44c)\n   b. Get audio playback position via sound callback\n   c. Compare position against buffer threshold\n   d. Clear audio playing flag when buffer exhausted\n5. Call SmackReadFrame() when ready to advance\n\nParameters:\n    pSmk - Pointer to Smacker video handle structure (Smack*)\n\nReturns:\n    1 - Frame was read, ready for display\n    0 - Not yet time for next frame, or video stopped/paused\n\nStructure Layout (Smacker handle offsets):\n    +0x3a8  dwStopped       - Non-zero if playback stopped\n    +0x41c  dwFrameReady    - Non-zero when frame timing satisfied\n    +0x420  dwNextFrameTime - Scaled timestamp for next frame (ms * 100)\n    +0x424  dwFrameInterval - Time between frames in scaled units\n    +0x428  apAudioBufs[7]  - Array of audio buffer pointers (7 tracks)\n    +0x444  nAudioTrack     - Active audio track index (-1 = none)\n    +0x448  dwAudioPlaying  - Non-zero if audio is playing\n    +0x44c  dwAudioPaused   - Non-zero if audio is paused\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    100 - Time scaling factor (milliseconds to internal units)\n    0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - Uninitialized next frame time marker\n    8 - Audio position margin for buffer comparison\n    0x3FF (>>10) - Audio buffer size field extraction mask",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
