      "name": "MemoryCopyRegions",
      "signature": "byte * MemoryCopyRegions(byte * pbDest, byte * pbSrcEnd, byte * pbSrc, int iDestEnd, uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "byte *",
      "comment": "Copies data from two memory regions into a destination buffer with wrap-around support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate bytes available in first region: iDestEnd - pbSrcEnd\n  2. If bytes available is less than or equal to total size and non-zero:\n     a. Copy dwBytesAvailable bytes from pbSrcEnd to pbDest using REP MOVSD/MOVSB\n     b. Reduce remaining size by bytes copied\n     c. Advance destination pointer\n  3. If remaining bytes to copy (dwSize) is non-zero:\n     a. Copy remaining bytes from pbSrc to current destination\n     b. Use REP MOVSD for dwords, REP MOVSB for remainder\n  4. Return pointer past end of copied data\n\nParameters:\n  pbDest    - byte*  - Destination buffer start address\n  pbSrcEnd  - byte*  - First source region pointer (typically buffer wrap point)\n  pbSrc     - byte*  - Second source region pointer (typically buffer start)\n  iDestEnd  - int    - End boundary of destination for size calculation\n  dwSize    - uint   - Total number of bytes to copy across both regions\n\nReturns:\n  byte* - Pointer to position after last copied byte (end of written data)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If dwBytesAvailable == 0, skips first region copy entirely\n  - If dwSize == 0 after first copy, skips second region copy\n  - Handles circular buffer wrap-around by splitting copy across two regions\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2 (SHR 2)  - Divide by 4 to get dword count\n  0x3 (AND 3)  - Mask to get remainder bytes (0-3)\n\nCallers:\n  UpdateAudioStreamBuffers, ProcessStreamQueue, ProcessSmackSoundQueue, ProcessSmackBufferList",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
