      "name": "InitializeMssSoundSystem",
      "signature": "bool InitializeMssSoundSystem(int pSmack)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Initializes the Miles Sound System (MSS) for Smacker video audio playback.\nLoads MSS32.DLL dynamically, validates version compatibility, and imports\nall required AIL (Audio Interface Library) function pointers for audio mixing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if MSS is already initialized via g_pListHead, return false if so\n  2. Store the Smacker handle in g_pSmackHandle for later use\n  3. If MSS callback not set, load MSS32.DLL with error mode suppression\n  4. Validate DLL handle is valid (must be >= 0x20, not error code)\n  5. Load version string from DLL resource ID 1 into buffer\n  6. Compare version against minimum required \"3.50F\" using __strcmpi\n  7. If version too old, show error MessageBox and fail\n  8. Import all AIL function pointers via GetProcAddress (22 functions)\n  9. Check AIL_get_preference(15) to determine audio mode capability\n  10. If preference returns 0, fall back to DirectSound via _SmackSoundUseDirectSound\n  11. Set up internal callback function pointers for stream processing\n  12. Set g_pfnSmackSoundCallback to internal MSS handler at LAB_10007d80\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack - Pointer to Smack structure containing video/audio configuration.\n           Field at offset 0x4C contains DirectSound fallback parameter.\n\nReturns:\n  true  - MSS initialized successfully or was already initialized with MSS\n  false - Initialization failed (DLL load error, version mismatch, no audio)\n\nError Handling:\n  SEM_FAILCRITICALERRORS (0x8000) suppresses DLL load error dialogs.\n  Version mismatch shows MessageBox with title \"Smacker Version Error\".\n  On failure, FreeLibrary is called and g_hMss32Dll is set to NULL.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x8000 - SEM_FAILCRITICALERRORS flag for SetErrorMode\n  0x20   - Minimum valid HINSTANCE value (below are system error codes)\n  0x0F   - AIL preference ID for checking audio capability\n  0x40   - Buffer size for version string (64 bytes)\n  0x4C   - Offset to DirectSound parameter in Smack structure",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
