      "name": "GetSmackSoundBufferSize",
      "signature": "dword GetSmackSoundBufferSize(int pSoundState)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Calculates the current audio buffer size for Smack sound playback.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Call FUN_10007c30() for initialization/synchronization\n  2. Get current system time via timeGetTime()\n  3. Calculate elapsed time: (currentTime - lastUpdateTime)\n  4. Scale the sample rate by elapsed time: (sampleRate * elapsed) / 1000\n  5. Cap the result to maxBufferSize: min(scaledSize, maxBufferSize)\n  6. Return: baseOffset + cappedSize\n\n  Parameters:\n  pSoundState (Stack[0x4]:4): Pointer to audio state structure\n    Offset 0x14: Sample rate (samples per second, DWORD)\n    Offset 0x7c: Last update timestamp (DWORD)\n    Offset 0x78: Maximum buffer size (DWORD)\n    Offset 0x60: Base buffer offset (DWORD)\n\n  Returns:\n  EAX: Current audio buffer size (baseOffset + scaledSamples)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
