      "name": "InitializeGameObject",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameObject(int nObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes a game object structure by zeroing specific fields and calling setup routines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load function pointer from g_pfnObjectInitCallback and call it with value at nObject+0x40\n  2. Clear EAX register to 0x00000000\n  3. Zero the field at offset 0x60 using cleared EAX value\n  4. Zero the field at offset 0x78 using cleared EAX value\n  5. Zero the field at offset 0x7c using cleared EAX value\n  6. Call FUN_10007ec0(nObject) to perform additional initialization setup\n  7. Return control to caller\n\nParameters:\n  nObject - Handle/pointer to object structure to initialize (int type, passed via ESP+0x8)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No value returned (EDX:EAX not used for return)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - The object must have valid callback handler at offset 0x40\n  - Function pointers at g_pfnObjectInitCallback must be properly initialized\n  - Three consecutive 4-byte fields are zeroed in sequence (0x60, 0x78, 0x7c)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
