      "comment": "Unlinks a node from a doubly-linked list structure\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if list is initialized (g_pListHead != 0)\n  2. Call cleanup callbacks for node fields at offsets 0x40, 0x68, 0x64\n  3. If node is list head, update head pointer to next node\n  4. Otherwise, traverse list from head until target node found\n  5. Update previous node's next pointer to skip target node\n\nParameters:\n  pNode - Pointer to node structure to unlink (passed in ESI)\n    Offset 0x3c: Next pointer in list\n    Offset 0x40: Field requiring cleanup callback\n    Offset 0x64: Field requiring cleanup callback\n    Offset 0x68: Field requiring cleanup callback\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Does nothing if list not initialized (g_pListHead == 0)\n  - Handles unlinking head node by updating global head pointer\n  - Safely handles node not found (traversal stops at NULL)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
