      "name": "SetSmackSampleVolumePan",
      "signature": "void SetSmackSampleVolumePan(uint pSmack, uint dwVolume)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the volume and pan for an MSS (Miles Sound System) audio sample.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Clamp dwVolume to maximum 0x8000 (32768)\n    2. Convert volume from Smacker range (0-0x8000) to AIL range (0-127):\n       - Formula: ((dwVolume * 0x4f6) / 0x8000 + 5) / 10\n       - 0x4f6 (1270) chosen so max input yields 127\n    3. Call AIL_set_sample_volume with sample handle from Smack+0x40\n    4. Convert pan from Smacker range (0-0x10000) to AIL range (0-127):\n       - Formula: ((dwPan * 0x4f6) / 0x10000 + 5) / 10\n    5. Call AIL_set_sample_pan with same sample handle\n\n  Parameters:\n    pSmack   - Pointer to Smack structure; sample handle at offset 0x40\n    dwVolume - Volume level (0-0x8000, clamped if exceeds max)\n    dwPan    - Pan position (0-0x10000; 0=left, 0x8000=center, 0x10000=right)\n\n  Returns:\n    void\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - Requires MSS library loaded via SmackSoundUseMSS\n    - g_pfnAIL_set_sample_volume and g_pfnAIL_set_sample_pan must be initialized\n    - Volume >0x8000 is silently clamped to 0x8000\n\n  Structure Layout (Smack audio-related fields):\n    Offset | Size | Field              | Type   | Description\n    0x40   | 4    | hAILSample         | HSAMPLE| AIL sample handle for MSS playback",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
