      "name": "_SmackSoundUseWin@0",
      "signature": "uint _SmackSoundUseWin@0(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Initializes Smack audio subsystem to use Windows waveOut API.\n\nExported as _SmackSoundUseWin@0 for external Smack library integration.\nSets up function pointer table for Windows multimedia audio output.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if sound handler already initialized (g_pfnSmackSoundHandler != NULL)\n2. If already initialized, return failure (AL=0)\n3. Otherwise, populate all sound callback function pointers:\n   - g_pfnSmackSoundInit -> ProcessSmackSoundQueue\n   - g_pfnSmackSoundHandler -> SmackSoundInitialize  \n   - g_pfnSmackSoundOpen -> RemoveSmackSoundNode\n   - g_pfnSmackSoundClose -> LAB_10008a30\n   - g_pfnSmackSoundMix -> ResetAudioOutput\n   - g_pfnCloseWaveOutCallback -> CloseWaveOutDeviceCallback\n   - g_pfnSoundOnCallback -> LAB_10008c90\n   - g_pfnSmackSoundCallback -> SetWaveOutVolumePan\n4. Return success (0x10008c01, AL=1)\n\nParameters:\n  None - This function takes no parameters (__stdcall with 0 bytes cleanup)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - On success: 0x10008c01 (low byte AL=1 indicates success)\n         On failure: masked handler address with AL=0 (already initialized)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Only one sound system can be active at a time (waveOut, DirectSound, or DirectWave)\n- Must be called before any Smack video with audio is opened\n- Thread-safe check via g_pfnSmackSoundHandler null test\n\nRelated Functions:\n- _SmackSoundUseDirectSound@4: Alternative using DirectSound\n- _SmackSoundUseDW@12: Alternative using DirectWave\n- InitializeMssSoundSystem: MSS/Miles Sound System alternative",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
