      "name": "OpenWaveOutDevice",
      "signature": "dword OpenWaveOutDevice(int nAudioContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Initialize waveOut audio device and prepare audio output buffers for playback\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Build WAVEFORMATEX structure from audio context: sample rate (0x48), \n     channels (0x54), bits per sample (0x50)\n  2. Check g_bDebugAudio flag and log \"Using standard waveOut\" if enabled\n  3. Call waveOutOpen with WAVE_MAPPER device (-1), format struct, and context callback\n  4. On success: initialize two audio buffers at offsets 0x64, 0x68\n  5. Clear buffer headers (32 bytes each) with memset\n  6. Prepare both wave headers via waveOutPrepareHeader\n  7. Generate silence pattern: 0x80 for 8-bit audio, 0x00 for 16-bit audio\n  8. Fill first buffer with silence using efficient DWORD writes\n  9. Call waveOutWrite to start playback\n  10. Poll timeGetTime with 1000ms timeout for WHDR_DONE flag on buffer\n  11. Return success (1) if playback completes, or call FUN_100089d0 if timeout\n\nParameters:\n  nAudioContext [ESP+0x04]  - Address of audio context structure\n                              Offset 0x40: HWAVEOUT device handle storage\n                              Offset 0x44: DWORD buffer size in bytes  \n                              Offset 0x48: DWORD sample rate (Hz)\n                              Offset 0x50: DWORD bits per sample (0=16-bit, other=8-bit)\n                              Offset 0x54: DWORD channel count minus 1\n                              Offset 0x64: LPWAVEHDR pointer to first buffer\n                              Offset 0x68: LPWAVEHDR pointer to second buffer\n                              Offset 0x78: DWORD callback flags\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 0x00000001  - Playback succeeded and completed within timeout\n  EAX = 0x00000000  - Playback completed (normal path)\n  EAX = MMRESULT    - waveOutOpen failed with specific MMSYSERR error code\n  \nSpecial Cases:\n  - No output device: waveOutOpen returns MMSYSERR_NODEVICE\n  - Device busy: waveOutOpen returns MMSYSERR_ALLOCATED\n  - Timeout occurs: Marks buffer with WHDR_DONE and calls cleanup function\n  - 8-bit audio: Uses 0x80 fill pattern, 16-bit uses 0x00 (silence)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
