      "name": "CloseWaveOutDevice",
      "signature": "void CloseWaveOutDevice(int nAudioContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Closes and cleans up the wave output device.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if wave output handle exists at offset 0x40\n  2. Call waveOutReset to reset the wave output device\n  3. Spin-wait for first wave header (offset 0x64) dwFlags & 1 to be set\n  4. Spin-wait for second wave header (offset 0x68) dwFlags & 1 to be set\n  5. Call waveOutUnprepareHeader for first buffer (offset 0x64)\n  6. Call waveOutUnprepareHeader for second buffer (offset 0x68)\n  7. Call waveOutClose to close wave output device\n  8. Set wave output handle to NULL\n\nParameters:\n  nAudioContext: Base address of audio context structure containing wave state\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If wave output handle is NULL, function returns immediately without cleanup",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:bd8059c7942cc3a5ef1a28c44257570a203103766f9cc2290acb102e791239fe",
