      "name": "ProcessSmackSoundQueue",
      "signature": "void ProcessSmackSoundQueue(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes Smack sound playback queue by writing audio data to wave device.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Iterate through linked list of Smack sound structures (g_pSmackSoundListHead)\n  2. For each sound, check if both input wave headers (0x64, 0x68) are ready (flag 0x1)\n  3. Validate buffer size > 3 bytes and select ready wave header\n  4. Copy audio data from sound buffer to wave header using MemoryCopyRegions\n  5. Update residual buffer size and clear ready flag from wave header (AND 0xfffffffe)\n  6. Fill remaining buffer space with silence bytes (0x80 for mono, duplicated for DWORD fills)\n  7. Submit filled wave header to waveOutWrite with size 0x20 (32)\n  8. Update timing counters: store current timestamp if first write, else track elapsed time\n  9. Calculate playback time in milliseconds: (dwBufferLength * 1000) / nSampleRate\n  10. Move to next sound in linked list via offset 0x3c\n\n  Parameters:\n  (none)\n\n  Returns:\n  (none)\n\n  Special Cases:\n  - Silence fill pattern: 0x80808080 for stereo/multi-byte, 0x80 for remaining bytes\n  - Mono vs stereo determined by field at offset 0x50 (0 = mono, 1 = stereo)\n  - Timing only updated if buffer successfully written\n  - Loop continues until linked list tail reached (puVar6 == NULL)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:7d7e2ef7622dbea270834b28127fe4b7c0167f326ae9f3988720e417d3eb6ae4",
