      "name": "ResetAudioOutput",
      "signature": "void ResetAudioOutput(int nAudioContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Resets audio output state and clears audio-related buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if HWAVEOUT handle at context offset 0x40 is non-NULL\n  2. If valid, invoke waveOutReset API to stop current playback\n  3. Zero all audio buffer state fields\n  4. Clear field at offset 0x60 (0x4)\n  5. Clear field at offset 0x6c (0x4)\n  6. Clear field at offset 0x70 (0x4)\n  7. Clear field at offset 0x74 (0x4)\n  8. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  nAudioContext: Pointer to audio context structure (passed via EDI per __stdcall)\n    Contains:\n      Offset +0x40 (size 4): HWAVEOUT handle for audio device\n      Offset +0x60 (size 4): Audio buffer pointer or state field\n      Offset +0x6c (size 4): Audio buffer state field\n      Offset +0x70 (size 4): Audio buffer state field\n      Offset +0x74 (size 4): Audio buffer state field\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If HWAVEOUT handle is NULL, waveOutReset is skipped\n  This function is typically called during audio subsystem shutdown",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:34e0c36d4ba339cfbd582b44c81408921c2b76f671490d190404c196d7e52985",
