      "name": "SetWaveOutVolumePan",
      "signature": "void SetWaveOutVolumePan(void * pSoundContext, uint dwVolume, uint dwPan)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets wave output volume with stereo panning for Smack audio playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Clamp volume to maximum 0xFFFF (65535)\n  2. Calculate left channel volume:\n     - If pan < 0x8000 (left bias): leftVol = volume * pan / 0x8000\n     - Otherwise: leftVol = volume (full)\n  3. Calculate right channel volume:\n     - If pan > 0x8000 (right bias): rightVol = volume * (0x10000 - pan) / 0x8000\n     - Otherwise: rightVol = volume (full)\n  4. Get wave device ID from HWAVEOUT at pSoundContext+0x40\n  5. Set stereo volume as packed DWORD: (leftVol << 16) | rightVol\n\nParameters:\n  pSoundContext - Pointer to sound context structure (HWAVEOUT at offset 0x40)\n  dwVolume      - Master volume level (0-0xFFFF, clamped if exceeded)\n  dwPan         - Stereo pan position:\n                  0x0000 = full left\n                  0x8000 = center (equal volume both channels)\n                  0xFFFF = full right\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Volume > 0xFFFF is clamped to 0xFFFF\n  - Pan == 0x8000 results in equal left/right volume (no panning applied)\n  - Pan < 0x8000 reduces left channel proportionally\n  - Pan > 0x8000 reduces right channel proportionally\n\nStructure Layout (pSoundContext):\n  Offset | Size | Field     | Type     | Description\n  0x40   | 4    | hWaveOut  | HWAVEOUT | Wave output device handle",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:96322149ac97dcb941c464edd1d486067362b3ca959c2c14bcb2fbf536dd7775",
