      "name": "SetDirectSoundHWND",
      "signature": "void SetDirectSoundHWND(int nHwnd)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the DirectSound window handle for audio playback coordination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store the provided window handle in g_hDirectSoundHWND global\n2. If g_pAudioManager is NULL, exit early (no audio system initialized)\n3. Acquire audio lock by incrementing g_dwAudioLockCount\n4. Call pre-lock callback via g_pfnAudioPreLock if set\n5. Invoke audio manager vtable method at offset 0x18 with hWnd and flags (0x2)\n6. Release audio lock by decrementing g_dwAudioLockCount\n7. Call post-lock callback via g_pfnAudioPostLock if set\n8. If debug mode enabled (g_bDebugAudio == 1):\n   - Convert result and hWnd to strings using __itoa (base 10)\n   - Output debug strings via OutputDebugStringA\n\nParameters:\n  nHwnd - Window handle (HWND) for DirectSound cooperative level\n          Stored in g_hDirectSoundHWND for later audio initialization\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; result logged to debug output if enabled\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if g_pAudioManager is NULL (audio not initialized)\n  - Debug output only when g_bDebugAudio flag is set to 1\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2     - DirectSound cooperative level flag passed to audio manager\n  0xa     - Radix for __itoa conversion (decimal)\n  0x18    - Vtable offset for SetCooperativeLevel-like method",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:bc0ec8aced85907df8d5b9e4552bf43a",
