      "name": "ProcessAudioStreamBuffer",
      "signature": "void ProcessAudioStreamBuffer(int * pAudioStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes an audio stream buffer for playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Extract audio parameters from input structure (frame count, size, flags)\n  2. Adjust frame byte count: pAudioStream[0x54] + 1 stored in wBytePerFrame\n  3. Load frame count from pAudioStream[0x48] into dwFrameCount\n  4. Calculate frame size: 0x10 if (pAudioStream[0x50]==0), else 0x18\n  5. Compute dwBufferBytes = wBytePerFrame * (wFrameSize >> 3) * dwFrameCount\n  6. Initialize request descriptor: dwRequestSize=0x14, dwRequestFlags=0x1\n  7. Atomic increment g_dwAudioLockCount for thread safety\n  8. Call g_pfnAudioPreLock callback if registered\n  9. Request buffer via g_pAudioManager->vtable[0xc](manager, pRequestDescriptor, abOutputBuffer)\n  10. If nAllocResult==0 (failure): call error handler and init buffer\n  11. Atomic decrement g_dwAudioLockCount\n  12. Call g_pfnAudioPostLock callback if registered\n\nParameters:\n  pAudioStream: Pointer to audio stream structure with fields:\n    +0x48: Frame count (uint, stored in dwFrameCount)\n    +0x50: Frame size selector flag (uint, 0=16-byte frame, else 24-byte)\n    +0x54: Frame byte offset adjustment (byte)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Operations handled via global callbacks and audio manager\n\nLocal Variables:\n  dwRequestSize: Request descriptor size field (0x14)\n  dwRequestFlags: Request descriptor flags (0x1)\n  dwReserved1-3: Zeroed reserved fields in request descriptor\n  wInitFlag: Format flag initialized to 1\n  wBytePerFrame: Bytes per frame (param[0x54] + 1)\n  wFrameSize: Frame size in bytes (0x10 or 0x18)\n  wBytesPerSample: Calculated bytes per sample\n  dwFrameCount: Total frame count from input\n  dwBufferBytes: Total buffer size in bytes\n  pRequestDescriptor: Pointer to request descriptor structure\n  nAllocResult: Return value from buffer allocation call\n  abOutputBuffer: Output buffer for allocation result (4 bytes, type limitation)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses atomic LOCK/UNLOCK operations on g_dwAudioLockCount\n  - Buffer allocation may fail (nAllocResult==0), triggering error handler\n  - Optional callbacks (g_pfnAudioPreLock/g_pfnAudioPostLock) are null-checked\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x14: Request descriptor structure size\n  0x10: Default frame size (16 bytes) when selector flag is 0\n  0x18: Extended frame size (24 bytes) when selector flag is 1\n  0xc: VTable offset for AllocateBuffer method\n  0x30: VTable offset for InitBuffer method\n  0x38: VTable offset for error handler",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
