      "name": "_SmackSoundUseDirectSound@4",
      "signature": "bool _SmackSoundUseDirectSound@4(undefined4 pAudioDevice)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Initializes DirectSound audio backend for Smack video playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store audio device pointer and reset initialization flag\n2. If sound handler already initialized, return whether it matches expected handler\n3. Suppress system error dialogs with SetErrorMode(SEM_FAILCRITICALERRORS)\n4. Dynamically load DSOUND.DLL using LoadLibraryA\n5. Restore original error mode\n6. Validate module handle (must be > 0x1F to indicate success)\n7. If load successful, resolve DirectSoundCreate function address\n8. Register all Smack audio callback function pointers\n9. If load failed, clear audio manager and return failure\n\nParameters:\n  pAudioDevice - Pointer to AudioDeviceContext for managing DirectSound state\n\nReturns:\n  true  - DirectSound initialized successfully or already initialized with correct handler\n  false - DSOUND.DLL failed to load (handle <= 0x1F)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x8000 - SEM_FAILCRITICALERRORS: Suppress critical error message boxes\n  0x1F   - Maximum error code; handles above this are valid module handles\n  0x20   - Minimum valid HMODULE value (first valid handle)\n\nError Handling:\n  SetErrorMode prevents system dialogs on missing DLL\n  Module handle validation catches LoadLibrary failures\n  On failure, g_pAudioManager reset to 0 to indicate uninitialized state",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:48fca3de7f9e4c3ef0fac22ed4260928",
