      "name": "InitializeAudioDevice",
      "signature": "BOOL InitializeAudioDevice(int pAudioContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "BOOL",
      "comment": "Initializes audio device and associated audio stream\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if audio stream already initialized (offset 0x60 of context)\n  2. If not initialized and g_dwAudioStreamCount is 0:\n     - Call InitializeDirectSoundAudio() to initialize DirectSound device\n     - Exit with error if initialization fails\n  3. Call InitializeAudioStream() with audio context\n  4. If stream initialization succeeds, increment g_dwAudioStreamCount via AcquireAudioLock()\n  5. Return initialization success code (0x01) or failure code (0x00)\n\nParameters:\n  pAudioContext: Pointer to AudioDeviceContext structure containing stream state at offset 0x60\n\nReturns:\n  0x01 (TRUE) on successful initialization\n  0x00 (FALSE) if DirectSound or stream initialization fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - First call initializes DirectSound device globally (g_dwAudioStreamCount tracks active streams)\n  - Subsequent calls reuse existing DirectSound device\n  - Audio stream may already be initialized (offset 0x60 != 0) on retry",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b6baa2c42034526c5e55bbcfd1854d448c858bca0c77cc13c1254acf62ae4f18",
