      "name": "ExpandByteToWord",
      "signature": "void ExpandByteToWord(int nUnused1, int nUnused2, uint * pDestBuffer, int nDestPitch, uint * pSrcBuffer, int nSrcPitch, uint dwWidth, int nHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Expands 8-bit byte pixels to 16-bit word pixels with line doubling for Smacker video playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate adjusted destination pitch for doubled rows (nDestPitch * 2 - dwWidth * 2)\n2. Check SIMD capability flag at 0x10015270 via DetectSIMDCapabilities\n3. If SIMD level > 1 (MMX/SSE available):\n   a. Process 16 bytes per iteration using MMX PUNPCKLBW/PUNPCKHBW\n   b. Write expanded words to both current row and next row (line doubling)\n   c. Handle remainder bytes (width & 0xF) with scalar loop\n4. If SIMD level <= 1 (scalar fallback):\n   a. Process 4 bytes per iteration with bit manipulation\n   b. Use SHR/ROR/SHL/OR to duplicate each byte into a word\n   c. Write to both current and next destination row\n5. Advance pointers by pitch values after each row\n6. Call EMMS before returning from MMX path\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused1 (ECX) - IMPLICIT: Unused register parameter (calling convention artifact)\n  nUnused2 (EDX) - IMPLICIT: Unused register parameter (calling convention artifact)  \n  pDestBuffer - Pointer to destination 16-bit pixel buffer\n  nDestPitch - Destination buffer row pitch in bytes\n  pSrcBuffer - Pointer to source 8-bit pixel buffer\n  nSrcPitch - Source buffer row pitch in bytes\n  dwWidth - Width in pixels to process per row\n  nHeight - Number of source rows to process (output is 2x rows)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero height: No processing performed\n  - Zero width: Inner loop skipped, only advances pointers\n  - Width not multiple of 16 (MMX path): Remainder pixels processed in scalar loop\n  - Width not multiple of 4 (scalar path): Remainder pixels processed individually\n\nPhantom Stack Variables (Assembly-Only):\n  local_44 [Stack[-0x44]:4] - Unused stack slot (reserved padding)\n  local_48 [Stack[-0x48]:4] - Unused stack slot (reserved padding)\n  local_4c [Stack[-0x4c]:4] - Unused stack slot (reserved padding)\n  local_50 [Stack[-0x50]:4] - Unused stack slot (reserved padding)\n\nStructure Layout (Stack Frame):\n  Offset  Size  Name              Description\n  -0x40   4     dwRowCount        Row counter for outer loop\n  -0x44   4     (reserved)        Unused stack padding\n  -0x48   4     (reserved)        Unused stack padding\n  -0x4c   4     (reserved)        Unused stack padding\n  -0x50   4     (reserved)        Unused stack padding\n\nMMX Register Usage:\n  MM0 - Source bytes / unpacked low words\n  MM1 - Source copy / unpacked high words\n  MM2 - Source bytes / unpacked low words (second qword)\n  MM3 - Source copy / unpacked high words (second qword)\n\nCalled By: _SmackBlit@44 (Smacker video blit routine)",
