      "name": "ExpandPixelDataDouble",
      "signature": "void ExpandPixelDataDouble(ushort * pDest, int nDestStride, uchar * pSrc, int nSrcStride, uint dwPixelCount, int nLineCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Expands 8-bit pixel data to 16-bit by duplicating each byte value.\n\nUsed for video frame upscaling - converts palettized/grayscale 8bpp pixels to 16bpp\nformat where each byte becomes a word (high byte = low byte). Called by SmackBlit\nfor Smacker video decompression output.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check SIMD capability level stored in global g_nSIMDLevel (0x10015270)\n2. If SIMD level unknown (0), call DetectSIMDCapabilities to determine MMX availability\n3. SCALAR PATH (no MMX, level <= 1):\n   a. Calculate 4-pixel chunks (dwPixelCount >> 2) and remainder (dwPixelCount & 3)\n   b. Process 4 pixels per iteration using bit manipulation:\n      - Load 4 source bytes as DWORD\n      - Extract individual bytes via ROR/SHR operations\n      - Duplicate each byte to form 16-bit words via SHL/OR\n      - Store two DWORDs (4 expanded pixels) to destination\n   c. Process remaining 0-3 pixels individually (MOV AL; MOV AH,AL; MOV [EDI],AX)\n   d. Advance source/dest pointers by stride, decrement line counter\n4. MMX PATH (level > 1):\n   a. Calculate 16-pixel chunks (dwPixelCount >> 4) and remainder (dwPixelCount & 0xF)\n   b. Process 16 pixels per iteration using MMX:\n      - MOVQ MM0/MM2: Load two 8-byte chunks (16 source pixels)\n      - PUNPCKLBW MM0,MM0 / PUNPCKHBW MM1,MM1: Expand bytes by duplicating\n      - Store four QWORDs (16 expanded pixels) to destination\n   c. Process remaining 0-15 pixels individually\n   d. Advance pointers, loop for each scanline\n5. EMMS to clear MMX state before return (MMX path only)\n\nParameters:\n  pDest       [ESP+0x04] - ushort*: Destination buffer for 16-bit expanded pixels\n  nDestStride [ESP+0x08] - int: Bytes to skip after each line in dest (stride - width*2)\n  pSrc        [ESP+0x0C] - uchar*: Source buffer of 8-bit pixels\n  nSrcStride  [ESP+0x10] - int: Bytes to skip after each line in source (stride - width)\n  dwPixelCount [ESP+0x14] - uint: Number of pixels per line to expand\n  nLineCount  [ESP+0x18] - int: Number of scanlines to process\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. Destination buffer filled with expanded pixels.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero pixel count: Loops execute zero times, only stride adjustment performed\n  - Zero line count: Outer loop never executes, immediate return\n  - Non-16-aligned count (MMX): Remainder loop handles 1-15 trailing pixels\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10015270 - g_nSIMDLevel global: 0=unknown, 1=no MMX, 2+=MMX available\n  0x3        - Mask for 4-pixel remainder (scalar path)\n  0xF        - Mask for 16-pixel remainder (MMX path)\n  0x8        - Bytes per 4 expanded pixels (scalar output stride)\n  0x20       - Bytes per 16 expanded pixels (MMX output stride, 32 bytes)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
