      "name": "BlitScaled2xWithColorTable",
      "signature": "void BlitScaled2xWithColorTable(ushort * pDstBuffer, int nDstPitch, byte * pSrcBuffer, int nSrcPitch, int nWidth, int nHeight, byte * pColorTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Blits an 8-bit indexed source buffer to a 16-bit destination with 2x scaling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate row advance values for src/dst buffers\n  2. For each row (nHeight iterations):\n    a. Initialize column counter to nWidth\n    b. Load first source pixel (AH) for interpolation\n  3. For each column (nWidth iterations):\n    a. Load current pixel (AL) forming 16-bit index in AX\n    b. Lookup two colors: table[(prevRow<<8)|currRow] for high byte,\n       table[(prevRow<<8)|prevCol] for low byte\n    c. Write combined 16-bit pixel to destination\n    d. Write second row pixel at nDstPitch offset using shifted index\n    e. Advance destination by 2 bytes\n  4. After each row:\n    a. Advance source by (nSrcPitch - nWidth)\n    b. Advance destination by 2*nDstPitch - 2*nWidth\n    c. Reset column pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pDstBuffer  - Destination 16-bit pixel buffer (EDI, RGB565/RGB555)\n  nDstPitch   - Destination row stride in bytes (stack+0xC)\n  pSrcBuffer  - Source 8-bit indexed pixels (ESI, EDX tracks current)\n  nSrcPitch   - Source row stride in bytes (stack+0x14)\n  nWidth      - Width in pixels to blit (stack+0x18)\n  nHeight     - Height in pixels to blit (stack+0x1C)\n  pColorTable - 256-entry color lookup table (EBP, 512 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Both nWidth and nHeight must be non-zero (caller validates)\n  - Uses bilinear-style interpolation via lookup table\n  - Two source pointers track current/previous for interpolation\n\nCalled From:\n  _SmackBlit@44 (0x1000b0bf) - Main Smacker video blitting routine",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
