      "name": "ExpandPaletteToDoublePixels",
      "signature": "void ExpandPaletteToDoublePixels(dword dwUnused, int nDestPitch, dword * pDest, int nSrcPitch, dword * pSrc, int nPaletteStride, dword dwWidth, dword dwHeight, ushort * pPaletteTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Expands 8-bit paletted pixel data to 16-bit doubled output for Smacker video rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate width32 = dwWidth >> 2 (full DWORDs to process)\n  2. Calculate remainder = dwWidth AND 3 (trailing pixels)\n  3. Check g_dwSIMDFeatureLevel at 0x10015270:\n     - 0: Call DetectSIMDCapabilities to determine capability\n     - 1: Use scalar code path (no MMX)\n     - 2+: Use SIMD code path (MMX MOVQ/PUNPCKLWD)\n  4. For each row (dwHeight times):\n     a. Process width32 DWORDs (4 pixels each):\n        - Load DWORD containing 4 byte indices\n        - Lookup each byte index in pPaletteTable (256-entry WORD table)\n        - Duplicate each 16-bit value: [val,val] forms 32-bit output\n        - Write 4 DWORDs (16 bytes) to destination\n     b. Process remainder (0-3) pixels individually\n     c. Advance: pDest += nSrcPitch, pSrc += nPaletteStride\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnused (ECX)       - Reserved/unused fastcall register parameter\n  nDestPitch (EDX)     - Destination buffer row pitch adjustment\n  pDest                - Output buffer (16-bit doubled pixels)\n  nSrcPitch            - Source data row pitch adjustment\n  pSrc                 - Input: packed 8-bit palette indices (4 per DWORD)\n  nPaletteStride       - Palette source row adjustment\n  dwWidth              - Width in pixels to process\n  dwHeight             - Number of rows to process\n  pPaletteTable        - WORD[256] lookup table mapping byte index to 16-bit pixel\n\nReturns:\n  void (implicitly returns via EAX:EDX but values are undefined)\n\nSIMD Path (g_dwSIMDFeatureLevel >= 2):\n  Uses MMX MOVD/PUNPCKLWD/MOVQ for 64-bit aligned writes\n  EMMS issued at function exit to clear MMX state\n\nCaller:\n  _SmackBlit@44 at 0x1000b1ab",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:a0fdaf893858add2983439be4e77b894cfb303becf34bbbda801f54508970ab9",
