      "name": "BlitIndexedToRGBA32",
      "signature": "void BlitIndexedToRGBA32(uint * pDest, int nDestPitch, byte * pSrc, int nSrcPitch, int nWidth, int nHeight, uint * pPalette)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Blit 8-bit indexed color pixels to 32-bit RGBA using palette lookup.\nPart of RAD Game Tools Smacker video codec. Converts indexed source pixels\nto full-color destination by looking up each byte pair in a 512-entry palette.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate row stride offsets for destination advancement\n  2. Initialize outer loop counter from nHeight\n  3. For each scanline (nYCount iterations):\n     a. Reset inner loop counter from nWidth\n     b. Load first source byte pair for palette indexing\n     c. For each pixel pair (nXCount iterations):\n        i. Read two source bytes (bSrcPixelA, bSrcPixelB)\n        ii. Combine into 16-bit index: (byteA << 8) | byteB\n        iii. Lookup palette entry via word[pPalette + index*2]\n        iv. Rotate and combine two 16-bit palette values into 32-bit DWORD\n        v. Write combined DWORD to destination buffer\n        vi. Repeat for complementary byte order (byteB, byteA)\n        vii. Advance destination by pitch, retreat by 4\n     d. Advance source pointer by (nSrcPitch - nWidth)\n     e. Advance destination pointer by calculated row offset\n  4. Return after all rows processed\n\nParameters:\n  pDest      - Pointer to destination pixel buffer (32-bit RGBA output)\n  nDestPitch - Destination row stride in bytes (typically width*4)\n  pSrc       - Pointer to source indexed pixel buffer (8-bit indices)\n  nSrcPitch  - Source row stride in bytes (typically width)\n  nWidth     - Image width in pixels (processed as pairs)\n  nHeight    - Image height in pixels (number of scanlines)\n  pPalette   - Pointer to 512-entry color lookup table (16-bit words)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Output written directly to pDest buffer\n\nStack Layout (phantom variables):\n  Offset   Size   Purpose\n  -0x30    4      local_30 - Scratch for dest pitch calculation\n  -0x34    4      local_34 - Scratch for dest pitch minus 4\n  -0x38    4      local_38 - Scratch for src pitch copy\n  -0x44    4      local_44 - Scratch for src pitch - width offset\n  -0x48    4      local_48 - Scratch for nHeight counter\n  -0x50    4      local_50 - Row offset accumulator\n\nCaller: _SmackBlit@44 (RAD Smacker video codec blit dispatcher)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
