      "name": "BlitMergeWithColorKey",
      "signature": "void BlitMergeWithColorKey(byte * pDest, int nDestPitch, byte * pSrc, int nSrcPitch, uint dwWidth, int nHeight, byte byColorKey, byte * pFallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Blits source to destination using color key transparency with MMX optimization.\n\nCopies pixels from source buffer to destination, substituting fallback pixels\nwhere source matches the color key. Uses MMX SIMD instructions when available\nand width >= 8 for 8x throughput improvement.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_dwSIMDFeatureLevel for MMX capability (>= 2)\n2. If MMX unavailable or width < 8, use scalar byte-by-byte loop\n3. For MMX path, broadcast colorKey to all 8 bytes of MM0\n4. Process 8 bytes per iteration using PCMPEQB mask generation\n5. PAND/PANDN/POR blend src with fallback based on mask\n6. Handle remaining (width % 8) bytes with scalar loop\n7. EMMS clears MMX state before return\n\nParameters:\n- pDest: Destination buffer pointer (receives blended output)\n- nDestPitch: Bytes to add after each row for destination stride\n- pSrc: Source buffer pointer (pixels to copy)\n- nSrcPitch: Bytes to add after each row for source stride\n- dwWidth: Number of pixels per row to process\n- nHeight: Number of rows to process\n- byColorKey: Transparent color value (0-255)\n- pFallback: Fallback buffer pointer (used where src == colorKey)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value, results written to pDest buffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Width < 8: Always uses scalar path regardless of MMX\n- SIMD level < 2: Falls back to scalar path\n- Width not multiple of 8: Remainder handled by scalar tail loop\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10015270: g_dwSIMDFeatureLevel global\n- 0x8: MMX minimum width / bytes per MMX iteration\n- 0x7: Mask for remainder calculation (width & 7)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
