      "name": "BlitMaskedBufferSIMD",
      "signature": "void BlitMaskedBufferSIMD(byte * pDest, int nDestStride, byte * pSrc, int nSrcStride, uint dwWidth, int nHeight, byte byMaskValue, byte * pMaskBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Masked buffer blit - conditionally copies source pixels based on mask.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Check SIMD level in g_dwSIMDFeatureLevel to enable MMX acceleration\n  2. If width >= 8 and MMX available: Process 8 bytes at a time\n     a. Broadcast byMaskValue to all 8 bytes of MMX register MM0\n     b. Load mask, source, and destination data into MMX registers\n     c. Compare mask bytes to byMaskValue using PCMPEQB (0xFF if match)\n     d. Use PAND/PANDN/POR to conditionally copy source bytes\n  3. Process remaining 0-7 pixels in scalar loop (byte-by-byte)\n  4. Advance pointers to next row and repeat for all nHeight rows\n\n  Parameters:\n    pDest (EDI, Stack[0x4]): Destination buffer, advanced by nDestStride per row\n    nDestStride (Stack[0x8]): Destination row pitch in bytes\n    pSrc (ESI, Stack[0xC]): Source buffer, advanced by nSrcStride per row\n    nSrcStride (Stack[0x10]): Source/mask row pitch in bytes\n    nWidth (EDX, Stack[0x14]): Width to process per row in bytes\n    nHeight (Stack[0x18]): Number of rows to process\n    byMaskValue (AH, Stack[0x1C]): Byte value in mask that indicates skip this pixel\n    pMaskBuffer (EBP, Stack[0x20]): Mask buffer (same layout as source)\n\n  Returns:\n    void - Updates destination buffer in-place\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - MMX path used only if nWidth >= 8 (0x8) and hardware supports it\n    - Falls back to scalar copy on non-MMX systems or narrow widths\n    - Register preservation: EDI, ESI, EBX saved and restored\n    - EMMS issued at function exit to clear MMX state",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
