      "name": "GetBlitScaleIndex",
      "signature": "uint GetBlitScaleIndex(uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Calculates the blit scale/mode index from SmackBlit configuration flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize result to 0\n  2. Check high bits (0xc0000000 - quality/precision flags)\n     - If set: result = 6 (higher quality mode base)\n  3. Check scaling bit 0x4\n     - If set: return result + 3 (fast path with additional scaling)\n  4. Check scaling bit 0x8\n     - If set: return result + 2 (alternative scaling mode)\n  5. Check scaling bit 0x2\n     - If set: increment result by 1\n  6. Return result\n\nParameters:\n  dwFlags (uint, Stack[0x4]) - Blit configuration flags\n    Bit 0x2: Basic scale increment\n    Bit 0x4: Triple-step scale (returns early with +3)\n    Bit 0x8: Double-step scale (returns early with +2)\n    Bits 0xc0000000: High-quality precision mode (adds 6 to base)\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Scale index 0-9 for SmackBlit operations\n    0: No scaling (base mode)\n    1: Basic scale (0x2 set)\n    2: Double-step scale (0x8 set)\n    3: Triple-step scale (0x4 set)\n    6: High-quality base (0xc0000000 set)\n    7: High-quality + basic (0xc0000000 + 0x2)\n    8: High-quality + double (0xc0000000 + 0x8)\n    9: High-quality + triple (0xc0000000 + 0x4)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early returns for bit 0x4 and 0x8 - checking order matters\n  - Bits 0x4 and 0x8 are mutually exclusive in return paths\n  - The scale index is used for SmackBlit table/palette selection\n\nCallers:\n  _SmackBlitOpen@4: Initializes blit structure, stores result at offset 0x14\n  _SmackBlitSetFlags@8: Updates blit flags dynamically, stores result at offset 0x14",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
