      "name": "_SmackBlitSetPalette@12",
      "signature": "void _SmackBlitSetPalette@12(uint * pBlitContext, byte * pbSourcePalette, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the palette for a Smack video blit context, reordering color channels based on flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if pVideoData is NULL (no palette buffer allocated)\n2. Calculate color channel offsets based on dwFlags:\n   - Default: R=0, G=1, B=2, stride=3 (packed RGB)\n   - Flag 0x4: Sets BGRA mode (stride=4)\n   - Flag 0x8 (with 0x4): Shifts to R=1, G=2, B=3 (skip alpha byte)\n   - Flag 0x2: Swaps red and blue channels (RGB <-> BGR)\n   - Flag 0x1: Doubles all offsets (16-bit color components)\n3. Convert 256 palette entries from source format to internal RGB format\n   - Loop copies bytes at calculated offsets into 768-byte local buffer\n4. Compare new palette with existing palette using REPE CMPSB (768 bytes)\n5. If palette changed OR force update flag set (offset 0x28):\n   - Increment frame counter (dwCurrentFrame)\n   - Copy new palette to context (192 DWORDs = 768 bytes)\n   - Call UpdateBlitContextPaletteAndFrame to apply changes\n   - Clear force update flag\n\nParameters:\n  pBlitContext    - SmackBlitContext* - Blit context containing palette buffer\n  pbSourcePalette - byte*             - Source palette data (256 colors)\n  dwFlags         - uint              - Color format flags:\n                    0x01 = 16-bit color components (double stride)\n                    0x02 = Swap R/B channels (BGR mode)\n                    0x04 = Include alpha byte (RGBA/BGRA stride=4)\n                    0x08 = Alpha byte first (with 0x04: skip first byte)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if pVideoData is NULL\n  - Skips copy if palette unchanged AND force flag not set\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x100 (256)  - Number of palette entries\n  0x300 (768)  - Total palette bytes (256 * 3 RGB)\n  0xC0  (192)  - DWORD count for palette copy (768 / 4)\n\nStructure Layout (SmackBlitContext offsets used):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x04    4     pVideoData      Pointer to palette data buffer\n  0x18    4     dwCurrentFrame  Frame counter, incremented on palette change\n  0x28    4     dwForceUpdate   Force palette update flag (cleared after update)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
