      "name": "_SmackBlitString@8",
      "signature": "char * _SmackBlitString@8(int pSmackBuffer, char * szOutputBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Returns a descriptive string for the current Smacker video blit mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read the blit mode type from pSmackBuffer offset 0x14\n2. Switch on mode (0-9) to select appropriate mode string:\n   - Case 0: \"8-bit 1x\" (no MMX suffix)\n   - Case 1: \"8-bit 2x\" (with MMX suffix)\n   - Case 2: \"8-bit 2x Interlaced\" (with MMX suffix)\n   - Case 3: \"8-bit 2x Smoothing\" (no MMX suffix)\n   - Case 6: \"16-bit 1x\" (no MMX suffix)\n   - Case 7: \"16-bit 2x\" (with MMX suffix)\n   - Case 8: \"16-bit 2x Interlaced\" (with MMX suffix)\n   - Case 9: \"16-bit 2x Smoothing\" (no MMX suffix)\n3. Copy the mode string to szOutputBuffer using MOVSD/MOVSB\n4. If MMX suffix is enabled and _SmackUseMMX@4(2) returns true:\n   - Find end of string using SCASB.REPNE\n   - Append \" using MMX\" suffix\n5. Return pointer to szOutputBuffer\n\nParameters:\npSmackBuffer (SmackBuffer*): Pointer to SmackBuffer structure with blit mode at offset 0x14\nszOutputBuffer (char*): Output buffer to receive the mode description string\n\nReturns:\nchar*: Pointer to szOutputBuffer containing the mode description\n\nMode String Layout:\nOffset 0x14 | String                    | MMX Suffix\n-----------|---------------------------|----------\n0          | \"8-bit 1x\"                | No\n1          | \"8-bit 2x\"                | Yes\n2          | \"8-bit 2x Interlaced\"     | Yes\n3          | \"8-bit 2x Smoothing\"      | No\n6          | \"16-bit 1x\"               | No\n7          | \"16-bit 2x\"               | Yes\n8          | \"16-bit 2x Interlaced\"    | Yes\n9          | \"16-bit 2x Smoothing\"     | No\n\nNote: Cases 4-5 are not handled (fall through to default)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:bac0004db822bf28b32d4daf991c1ac2",
