      "name": "_SmackBlit@44",
      "signature": "int _SmackBlit@44(void * pBlitContext, void * pDestBuffer, int nDestPitch, int nDestX, int nDestY, void * pSrcBuffer, int nSrcPitch, int nSrcX, int nSrcY, uint nWidth, uint nHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Dispatches Smacker video frame data to the appropriate blit routine based on pixel format mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dimensions - return early if width or height is zero\n2. Read blit mode from context structure at offset 0x14\n3. Calculate source and destination buffer offsets using pitch and coordinates\n4. Route to appropriate blit routine based on mode:\n   - Mode 0: Direct 16-bit copy (CopyBitmapRegion)\n   - Mode 1: 8-bit to 16-bit expansion (ExpandByteToWord)\n   - Mode 2: Double pixel expansion (ExpandPixelDataDouble)\n   - Mode 3: 2x scaled with color table (BlitScaled2xWithColorTable)\n   - Mode 6: 8-bit palettized to 16-bit (BlitPalettized8to16)\n   - Mode 7: Indexed to dual 16-bit buffer (ConvertIndexedPixelsToDualBuffer16)\n   - Mode 8: Palette to double pixels (ExpandPaletteToDoublePixels)\n   - Mode 9: Indexed to RGBA32 (BlitIndexedToRGBA32)\n\nParameters:\n  pBlitContext - Smacker blit context structure containing:\n                 +0x0C: color table/palette pointer (modes 3, 9)\n                 +0x10: palette pointer (modes 6, 7, 8)\n                 +0x14: blit mode (0-9)\n  pDestBuffer  - Destination pixel buffer base address\n  nDestPitch   - Destination buffer pitch in bytes per scanline\n  nDestX       - X offset in destination buffer\n  nDestY       - Y offset (row) in destination buffer\n  pSrcBuffer   - Source pixel buffer base address\n  nSrcPitch    - Source buffer pitch in bytes per scanline\n  nSrcX        - X offset in source buffer\n  nSrcY        - Y offset (row) in source buffer\n  nWidth       - Width of region to blit in pixels\n  nHeight      - Height of region to blit in scanlines\n\nReturns:\n  EAX from blit subroutine on success, or original context pointer if dimensions are zero\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero width or height: Returns immediately without blitting\n  - Modes 4, 5: Fall through without processing (unsupported modes)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x14 - Offset to blit mode in context structure\n  0x0C - Offset to color table pointer\n  0x10 - Offset to palette pointer",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
