      "name": "_SmackBlitClear@32",
      "signature": "void _SmackBlitClear@32(uint * pBlitInfo, int nDestBuffer, int nPitch, int nBytesPerPixel, int nRowPitch, uint dwWidth, int nHeight, uint dwColorIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Clears a rectangular region in a Smacker video frame buffer with a solid color.\n\nSupports both 8-bit (1 byte per pixel) and 16-bit (2 bytes per pixel) color modes,\ndetermined by the top two bits of the blit info structure. Uses optimized REP STOS\ninstructions to fill rows 4 bytes at a time, then handles remaining bytes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract mode flags from pBlitInfo[0] (bits 30-31)\n2. Resolve color index: if negative, negate; if palette mode, lookup from pBlitInfo[4] table\n3. Calculate destination pointer: nDestBuffer + (bytesPerPixel * nBytesPerPixel) + (nPitch * nRowPitch)\n4. For 8-bit mode (dwModeFlags == 0):\n   a. Fill 4 pixels at a time using DWORD writes (dwWidth >> 2)\n   b. Fill remaining 1-3 pixels with single byte writes (dwWidth & 3)\n   c. Advance to next row by adding nPitch\n5. For 16-bit mode (dwModeFlags != 0):\n   a. Fill 2 pixels at a time using DWORD writes (dwWidth >> 1)\n   b. Fill remaining 0-1 pixel with word write (dwWidth & 1)\n   c. Advance to next row by adding nPitch\n\nParameters:\n  pBlitInfo - Pointer to blit info structure; [0]=mode flags, [4]=palette table pointer\n  nDestBuffer - Base address of destination frame buffer\n  nPitch - Row stride in bytes (distance between row starts)\n  nBytesPerPixel - Bytes per pixel (1 or 2)\n  nRowPitch - Vertical position multiplier for row offset calculation\n  dwWidth - Width of rectangle to clear in pixels\n  nHeight - Height of rectangle to clear in rows\n  dwColorIndex - Color index (or negative raw value)\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xC0000000 - Mask for mode flags (bits 30-31)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nHeight is 0, function returns immediately without filling\n  - Negative dwColorIndex: uses absolute value as raw color\n  - Non-zero mode flags: looks up color from palette table at pBlitInfo[4]",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b9fd0d60117cd74f98d6dc73a1ae2d29300f2cc54b623a811cf051fde16d136e",
