      "name": "_SmackBufferToBufferTrans@36",
      "signature": "void _SmackBufferToBufferTrans@36(int * pDestBuffer, int nDestX, uint dwDestY, int * pSrcBuffer, int nSrcX, uint dwSrcY, uint dwWidth, int nHeight, byte byColorKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Copies a rectangular region from source SmackBuffer to destination SmackBuffer with transparency.\nPerforms transparent blit using a color key - pixels matching the color key are skipped.\nUses BlitTransparent_SIMD for the actual pixel copying with MMX/SSE optimization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Validate pDestBuffer and pSrcBuffer pointers; early exit if either is NULL\n  2. Check buffer type flags at offset 0x00 of each SmackBuffer\n  3. Calculate source and destination row strides based on buffer widths\n  4. Compute effective clipping based on buffer dimensions and requested region\n  5. Calculate source pixel address: pSrcBuffer->pPixels + (dwSrcY * stride) + nSrcX\n  6. Calculate dest pixel address: pDestBuffer->pPixels + (dwDestY * stride) + nDestX\n  7. Call BlitTransparent_SIMD with computed addresses, strides, dimensions, and color key\n\nParameters:\n  pDestBuffer - Destination SmackBuffer containing target pixel buffer\n  nDestX - X offset in destination buffer (signed for clipping)\n  dwDestY - Y offset in destination buffer\n  pSrcBuffer - Source SmackBuffer containing source pixel data\n  nSrcX - X offset in source buffer (signed for clipping)\n  dwSrcY - Y offset in source buffer\n  dwWidth - Width of region to copy in pixels\n  nHeight - Height of region to copy in rows\n  byColorKey - Transparent color value (pixels with this value are not copied)\n\nReturns:\n  void (modifies destination buffer in-place)\n\nStructure Layout (SmackBuffer offsets used):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  0x00    4     dwFlags       Buffer type/state flags\n  0x14    4     nWidth        Buffer width in pixels\n  0x18    4     nStride       Row stride in bytes\n  0x448   4     pPixels       Pointer to pixel data buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL buffer pointers: Function returns immediately without operation\n  - Zero flags at offset 0x00: Alternate stride calculation path used\n  - Clipping handled via signed X coordinates and stride adjustments",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d4898204a8cafa5b613c36834bc8035d7cb9e65a44b3f9a3f3f179224bb89105",
