      "comment": "Copies a rectangular region from source buffer to destination buffer using a mask buffer.\nOnly pixels where the mask matches byMaskValue are copied. Supports flipped (bottom-up) buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate source and destination buffers are non-null\n2. Verify buffer format compatibility (pixel format and bytes per pixel must match)\n3. Calculate adjusted coordinates based on buffer orientation (top-down vs bottom-up)\n4. Compute source and destination memory offsets using stride * Y + base pointer\n5. Call BlitMaskedBufferSIMD to perform the actual masked pixel copy\n\nParameters:\n  pDestBuf     - Pointer to destination SmackBuf structure\n  nDestX       - X offset in destination buffer (signed for left/right positioning)\n  dwDestY      - Y offset in destination buffer\n  pSrcBuf      - Pointer to source SmackBuf structure\n  nSrcX        - X offset in source buffer (signed for left/right positioning)\n  dwSrcY       - Y offset in source buffer\n  dwWidth      - Width of region to copy in pixels\n  nHeight      - Height of region to copy (signed for direction)\n  byMaskValue  - Mask comparison value (pixels matching this are copied)\n  pMaskBuf     - Pointer to mask SmackBuf structure\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSmackBuf Structure Offsets Used:\n  +0x00  - Pixel format identifier (must match between buffers)\n  +0x14  - Buffer width in pixels\n  +0x18  - Bytes per pixel (must match between buffers)\n  +0x448 - Pointer to raw pixel data\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if pSrcBuf or pSrcBuf is NULL\n  - Returns early if pixel formats don't match\n  - Returns early if bytes per pixel don't match\n  - Handles inverted (bottom-up) buffers via coordinate negation",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
