      "name": "ConvertUintToString",
      "signature": "void ConvertUintToString(uint dwValue, char * szBuffer, uint dwRadix, int nIsNegative)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts an unsigned integer to a null-terminated ASCII string in the specified radix.\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 1998 Release (_xtoa)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nIsNegative is set, write '-' character and negate dwValue\n2. Enter digit extraction loop:\n   a. Compute remainder = dwValue % dwRadix\n   b. Convert remainder to ASCII: '0'-'9' for 0-9, 'a'-'z' for 10-35\n   c. Store digit at current position, advance pointer\n   d. Divide dwValue by dwRadix for next iteration\n   e. Repeat while dwValue != 0\n3. Null-terminate the string\n4. Reverse the digit portion in-place using two-pointer swap\n\nParameters:\n  dwValue      (uint)   - Value to convert (treated as unsigned)\n  szBuffer     (char*)  - Output buffer for the string representation\n  dwRadix      (uint)   - Numeric base for conversion (2-36)\n  nIsNegative  (int)    - Non-zero if original value was negative\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result is written to szBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - dwValue = 0 produces \"0\"\n  - Radix 10 with nIsNegative produces negative decimal string\n  - Radix 16 produces lowercase hexadecimal ('a'-'f')\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x2d ('-')  - Minus sign for negative numbers\n  0x30 ('0')  - ASCII digit zero, base for 0-9\n  0x57 ('W')  - Base offset for a-z (0x57 + 10 = 'a')\n  0x9         - Threshold: digits 0-9 vs a-z",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
