      "name": "SwapMemoryBytes",
      "signature": "void SwapMemoryBytes(byte * pbSrc, byte * pbDst, int nByteCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Swaps memory contents between two byte buffers of specified size.\n\nLibrary Function: Visual Studio 1998 Release (_swap)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if source and destination pointers are equal - exit early if so\n2. Check if byte count is zero - exit early if so\n3. Loop through each byte position:\n   a. Read byte from source into temporary\n   b. Copy byte from destination to source\n   c. Copy temporary to destination\n   d. Advance both pointers\n   e. Decrement counter and repeat until zero\n\nParameters:\n  pbSrc - Pointer to first memory buffer (byte *)\n  pbDst - Pointer to second memory buffer (byte *)\n  nByteCount - Number of bytes to swap between buffers (int)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, buffers are modified in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pbSrc == pbDst, function returns immediately (no-op)\n  - If nByteCount == 0, function returns immediately (no-op)\n  - Buffers must not overlap or results are undefined\n\nCallers:\n  - QuickSortPartitionThreeWay (0x1000bc8e, 0x1000bcd1, 0x1000bcdc)\n  - QuickSortPartition (0x1000bda5)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
