      "name": "_tolower",
      "signature": "int _tolower(int nChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts an uppercase character to lowercase using locale-aware mapping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If ANSI code page is 0 (default C locale), use fast ASCII-only path\n   - If character is in range 'A'-'Z' (0x41-0x5A), add 0x20 to convert to lowercase\n   - Return the character unchanged otherwise\n2. For single-byte characters (< 0x100), check if character is uppercase\n   - Use character type table lookup if g_nMbCurMax < 2 (single-byte locale)\n   - Use __isctype() call with CT_UPPER (1) flag for multi-byte locales\n   - If not uppercase, return character unchanged\n3. For multi-byte or uppercase single-byte characters:\n   - Extract high byte and low byte from input character\n   - Check if high byte indicates lead byte of multi-byte character (0x80 bit)\n   - If single-byte: set up 1-byte source buffer\n   - If multi-byte: set up 2-byte source buffer with lead/trail bytes\n4. Call MapLocaleStringWithCodePage() with LCMAP_LOWERCASE (0x100) flag\n5. Return the converted character:\n   - Original character if mapping failed (return 0)\n   - Low byte of wide char buffer if result is 1 character\n   - Full wide char value if result is multi-byte\n\nParameters:\n    nChar: int - Character to convert (can be single-byte ASCII or multi-byte)\n\nReturns:\n    int - Lowercase equivalent of the input character\n          Returns original character if already lowercase or not alphabetic\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n    0x41 (65)   - ASCII 'A', start of uppercase range\n    0x5A (90)   - ASCII 'Z', end of uppercase range\n    0x20 (32)   - Difference between uppercase and lowercase ASCII\n    0x100 (256) - Boundary for single-byte vs extended characters\n                  Also LCMAP_LOWERCASE flag for LCMapString\n    0x80        - Lead byte indicator in multi-byte character type table\n    1           - CT_UPPER flag for __isctype() check\n    3           - Maximum wide char buffer size for output\n\nStack Layout (ESP+offset):\n    Offset  Size  Variable       Purpose\n    0x04    4     nChar          Input character parameter\n    -0x02   1     bTerminator    Null terminator for 2-byte source\n    -0x03   1     bLowByte       Low/trail byte of character\n    -0x04   1     bHighByte      High/lead byte of character\n    -0x08   4     awWideCharBuf  WCHAR[2] output buffer\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n    g_nAnsiCodePage (0x10015338): Current ANSI code page (0 = C locale)\n    g_nMbCurMax (0x10015864): Max bytes per character in current locale\n    g_pCTypeTable (0x10015658): Pointer to character type classification table",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
