      "name": "__cinit",
      "signature": "void __cinit(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Executes C/C++ runtime static initializers during program startup.\n\nThis is a Visual Studio 1998 CRT library function that initializes global\nand static objects before main() is called. It processes two initializer\ntables: one for C++ constructors and one for C static initializers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pre-initialization callback (g_pfnPreCInit) is registered\n2. If callback exists, invoke it for early initialization\n3. Call __initterm on C++ initializer table (g_ppfnCppInitStart to g_ppfnCppInitEnd)\n4. Call __initterm on C initializer table (g_ppfnCInitStart to g_ppfnCInitEnd)\n5. Return result from last __initterm call\n\nParameters:\n  None - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  int - Return value from last __initterm call (typically 0 on success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Pre-init callback may be NULL if no early initialization is needed\n  - Initializer tables may be empty (start == end pointers)\n  - Called once during CRT startup before main()\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_pfnPreCInit (0x10015fac) - Optional pre-initialization callback pointer\n  g_ppfnCppInitStart (0x10014008) - Start of C++ static constructor table\n  g_ppfnCppInitEnd (0x1001400c) - End of C++ static constructor table\n  g_ppfnCInitStart (0x10014000) - Start of C static initializer table\n  g_ppfnCInitEnd (0x10014004) - End of C static initializer table",
