      "name": "__initterm",
      "signature": "void __initterm(void * * ppfnStart, void * * ppfnEnd)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Iterates through a table of function pointers and calls each non-null entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare start pointer against end pointer\n2. If start >= end, exit immediately (empty table)\n3. Loop: Load function pointer from current table entry\n4. If function pointer is non-null, call the function\n5. Advance table pointer by one entry (4 bytes)\n6. If current position < end, continue loop\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  ppfnStart (void**) - Pointer to start of function pointer table\n  ppfnEnd (void**) - Pointer to end of function pointer table (exclusive)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty table (start >= end): Returns immediately without executing any functions\n  - Null function pointer entries: Skipped without calling\n\nNotes:\n  This is a CRT library function from Visual Studio 1998 used for static\n  initialization (__initterm) and termination (__initterm_e). Called during\n  DLL/EXE startup to invoke C++ static constructors and atexit handlers.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
