      "name": "InitializeStdioHandles",
      "signature": "void InitializeStdioHandles(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes the standard I/O handle table for process stdio/stdout/stderr.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Allocate 0x100 byte handle entry block (32 entries, 8 bytes each)\n  2. Initialize entries with handle=-1 (0xFFFFFFFF) and flags=0x0A (unused)\n  3. Allocate additional 0x100 byte blocks if inherited handles exceed 32 (up to 0x800 max)\n  4. Process inherited handles from STARTUPINFOA.lpReserved2 if present\n  5. Map inherited handle bits to handle table entries\n  6. Initialize standard handles (stdin, stdout, stderr) with GetStdHandle\n  7. Set handle flags based on file type (disk=0x80, pipe=0x40, char=0x08)\n  8. Call SetHandleCount with final handle table size\n\nParameters:\n  None (uses global g_pHandleTable, g_dwHandleCount, g_pHandleTableExt)\n\nReturns:\n  void (exits via __amsg_exit(0x1B) if memory allocation fails)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Handles count clamped to 0x800 (2048) maximum\n  - Inherited handle bits limited by 0x1F mask (32 handles per block)\n  - Handle type detection via GetFileType (0x02=pipe, 0x03=char device)\n  - Standard handles (indices 0-2) initialized even if not inherited",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:f249d5c0adc13614ae63f991f978ac70265d17dc034a26803020ff5497d43e78",
