      "name": "CleanupHandleTable",
      "signature": "void CleanupHandleTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Frees all allocated heap memory for handle table entries\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize pointer to start of handle table (0x10015ea0)\n  2. Loop through each handle entry until end of table (0x10015fa0)\n  3. For each non-NULL handle pointer, call FreeHeapMemory to release memory\n  4. Advance to next handle entry (increment by 4 bytes)\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Handles NULL entries by skipping them (TEST/JZ instruction)\n  - Handles empty table gracefully if start equals end address",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
