      "name": "__setargv",
      "signature": "int __setargv(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes the argument vector (argv) and argument count (argc) for the C runtime.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetModuleFileNameA to retrieve the executable path into g_szModuleFilename buffer\n2. Check if command line buffer (g_szCmdLineBuffer) is empty\n3. If empty, use module filename as program name; otherwise use command line buffer\n4. Store program name pointer in g_pszProgramName\n5. First pass: Call ParseCommandLineArgs to count arguments and calculate required buffer size\n6. Calculate total allocation: (argc * sizeof(char*)) + string buffer size\n7. Call AllocateMemoryWithRetry to allocate combined buffer for argv array and strings\n8. If allocation fails, call __amsg_exit(8) to terminate with out-of-memory error\n9. Second pass: Call ParseCommandLineArgs to populate argv array and copy argument strings\n10. Decrement argc by 1 (exclude NULL terminator from count)\n11. Store final argv pointer in g_ppszArgv and argc in g_nArgc\n\nParameters:\nNone - uses global state from command line initialization\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns (argc - 1), the number of command line arguments excluding program name\n\nGlobals Modified:\ng_szModuleFilename (0x10015d68) - Receives executable path from GetModuleFileNameA\ng_pszProgramName (0x10015384) - Set to point to program name string\ng_ppszArgv (0x1001536c) - Set to allocated argv array\ng_nArgc (0x10015368) - Set to argument count\n\nError Handling:\nIf memory allocation fails, calls __amsg_exit(8) which terminates the process.\nError code 8 indicates R6008 \"not enough space for arguments\".",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
