      "name": "ParseCommandLineArgs",
      "signature": "void ParseCommandLineArgs(char * lpszCmdLine, char * * lpszArgvOut, char * lpszArgBuffer, int * pnCharCount, int * pnArgCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Parses a command-line string into individual arguments following Windows conventions.\nHandles quoted strings, backslash escapes, and MBCS lead bytes correctly.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize character count to 0 and argument count to 1\n2. If argv output array provided, store pointer to first argument\n3. Parse program name (first argument):\n   a. If starts with quote (0x22), parse as quoted string until closing quote\n   b. Otherwise, parse until whitespace (space 0x20 or tab 0x09)\n   c. Handle MBCS lead bytes by copying both bytes of multibyte characters\n4. Skip whitespace between arguments\n5. For each subsequent argument:\n   a. Store argument pointer in argv array if provided\n   b. Increment argument count\n   c. Process backslash sequences before quotes (2N backslashes -> N, 2N+1 -> N plus literal quote)\n   d. Toggle quote mode on unescaped quotes; inside quotes, two quotes -> one literal quote\n   e. Copy characters to output buffer, handling MBCS lead bytes\n   f. Terminate on whitespace outside quotes or end of string\n6. Null-terminate final argv entry if array provided\n7. Increment final argument count for null terminator slot\n\nParameters:\n    lpszCmdLine - Input command-line string to parse\n    lpszArgvOut - Output array of argument pointers (NULL if only counting)\n    lpszArgBuffer - Output buffer for null-terminated argument strings (NULL if only counting)\n    pnCharCount - Output: total character count including null terminators\n    pnArgCount - Output: total argument count including null terminator slot\n\nReturns:\n    void - Results returned through output pointer parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - Quoted strings preserve embedded spaces and tabs\n    - Backslash escaping only applies before double quotes\n    - Adjacent quotes inside quoted string produce single literal quote\n    - MBCS lead bytes (bit 0x04 in g_abMbcsLeadByteTable) cause next byte to be copied as pair\n    - First pass with NULL pointers counts required buffer sizes\n    - Second pass with allocated buffers performs actual parsing\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x22 - Double quote character\n    0x5C - Backslash character  \n    0x20 - Space character\n    0x09 - Tab character\n    0x04 - MBCS lead byte flag in character type table",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
