      "name": "GetSystemCodePage",
      "signature": "uint GetSystemCodePage(int nCodePageSelector)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Resolves a code page selector constant to an actual Windows code page identifier.\n\nThis is a CRT library function (_getSystemCP) from Visual Studio 1998 Release that\ntranslates special negative code page selector values into actual code page numbers\nby calling Windows API functions or returning a default code page.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SBCS fallback flag to disabled (0)\n2. Check if selector is CP_OEMCP (-2):\n   a. Enable SBCS fallback flag\n   b. Return result of GetOEMCP() - system OEM code page\n3. Check if selector is CP_ACP (-3):\n   a. Enable SBCS fallback flag  \n   b. Return result of GetACP() - system ANSI code page\n4. Check if selector is CP_THREAD_ACP (-4):\n   a. Enable SBCS fallback flag\n   b. Return cached default code page from g_dwDefaultCodePage\n5. Otherwise: return the selector unchanged (assumed to be valid code page ID)\n\nParameters:\n  nCodePageSelector - Code page selector, one of:\n    -2 (CP_OEMCP): Request OEM code page via GetOEMCP()\n    -3 (CP_ACP): Request ANSI code page via GetACP()  \n    -4 (CP_THREAD_ACP): Request thread's default code page\n    >0: Direct code page identifier (returned unchanged)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Resolved Windows code page identifier:\n    - OEM code page (typically 437 or 850) if selector was -2\n    - ANSI code page (typically 1252) if selector was -3\n    - Cached default code page if selector was -4\n    - Original selector value if positive (passthrough)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  -2 (0xFFFFFFFE): CP_OEMCP - OEM code page constant\n  -3 (0xFFFFFFFD): CP_ACP - ANSI code page constant\n  -4 (0xFFFFFFFC): CP_THREAD_ACP - Thread code page constant\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_fSbcsFallbackEnabled (0x100154bc): Flag set to 1 when using system code page\n  g_dwDefaultCodePage (0x10015348): Cached default code page value\n  g_pfnGetOEMCP (0x1001629c): Function pointer to kernel32!GetOEMCP\n  g_pfnGetACP (0x100162ac): Function pointer to kernel32!GetACP",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
