      "name": "_CPtoLCID",
      "signature": "dword _CPtoLCID(dword dwCodePage)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Converts a Windows Code Page identifier to its corresponding Locale ID (LCID).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Subtract base code page value (0x3a4/932) from input to get switch index\n2. If index > 18 (0x12), return 0 indicating unsupported code page\n3. Use jump table at 0x1000ca68 with index byte array at 0x1000ca7c\n4. Return the corresponding LCID for supported East Asian code pages\n\nParameters:\n  dwCodePage (dword) - Windows Code Page identifier to convert\n\nReturns:\n  dword - Locale ID (LCID) if code page is supported, 0 otherwise\n    0x411 (1041) - Japanese locale for CP 932 (0x3a4)\n    0x804 (2052) - Simplified Chinese locale for CP 936 (0x3a8)\n    0x412 (1042) - Korean locale for CP 949 (0x3b5)\n    0x404 (1028) - Traditional Chinese locale for CP 950 (0x3b6)\n    0 - Unsupported code page\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  Code Pages:\n    0x3a4 (932)  - Japanese Shift-JIS\n    0x3a8 (936)  - Simplified Chinese GBK\n    0x3b5 (949)  - Korean EUC-KR\n    0x3b6 (950)  - Traditional Chinese Big5\n  Locale IDs:\n    0x411 (1041) - Japanese (Japan)\n    0x804 (2052) - Chinese (PRC)\n    0x412 (1042) - Korean (Korea)\n    0x404 (1028) - Chinese (Taiwan)\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 1998 Release CRT",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:4ba71d3b2af8f713a4489ef466e851531b95ef95062dc6dd6b916181739fae84",
