      "name": "setSBCS",
      "signature": "undefined setSBCS(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Resets the runtime to Single-Byte Character Set (SBCS) mode.\n\nClears all multibyte character set (MBCS) state by zeroing the character\ntype lookup table and resetting code page configuration globals. Called\nduring CRT initialization or when switching from MBCS to SBCS mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero 257 bytes (0x101) of g_abMbcType character type lookup table\n   - Uses REP STOSD for 64 dwords (256 bytes) + STOSB for final byte\n2. Clear g_stMbCodePageInfo structure base pointer\n3. Clear g_dwCurrentCodePage (active code page identifier)\n4. Clear g_dwLocaleId (locale identifier for MBCS operations)\n5. Clear g_dwMbCodePageField1 and g_dwMbCodePageField2 (reserved fields)\n\nParameters:\n   None - operates on global MBCS state variables\n\nReturns:\n   void - no return value, always succeeds\n\nDecompiler SSA Variables (compiler-generated, cannot be renamed):\n   iVar1 (nLoopCounter) - ECX register, loop counter for REP STOSD (64 iterations)\n   puVar2 (pdwDestPtr) - EDI register, destination pointer for STOSD/STOSB\n\nMagic Numbers:\n   0x40 (64) - Number of dwords to clear (256 bytes / 4)\n   0x100153a0 - g_abMbcType base address (257-byte character type table)\n   0x100154b0 - g_stMbCodePageInfo base address\n\nRelated Functions:\n   SetMultibyteCodePage - Caller that switches to MBCS mode\n   _setmbcp - CRT function for setting multibyte code page",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
