      "name": "DisplayRuntimeError",
      "signature": "void DisplayRuntimeError(int nErrorCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Displays a runtime error message based on error code lookup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search error code table (g_aErrorCodeTable) for matching nErrorCode\n2. If found and in console mode (g_dwErrorHandlingMode == 1 or NT initialized):\n   a. Get console handle from g_pHandleTable[4] or GetStdHandle(STD_ERROR_HANDLE)\n   b. Write error string to console via WriteFile\n3. If found and in dialog mode:\n   a. Skip if error code is 0xfc (no-op sentinel)\n   b. Get module filename via GetModuleFileNameA\n   c. If path unavailable, use \"<program name unknown>\"\n   d. If path > 60 chars, truncate and append \"...\"\n   e. Build message: \"Runtime Error!\n\nProgram: [path]\n\n[error text]\"\n   f. Display via ___crtMessageBoxA with MSVC Runtime Library title\n\nParameters:\n  nErrorCode - CRT runtime error code to look up in error table\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Error code 0xfc (252) is a no-op sentinel, produces no output\n  - Invalid error codes (not in table) produce no output\n  - Long module paths (>60 chars) are truncated with ellipsis\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x100155c0 - g_aErrorCodeTable base address\n  0x10015648 - g_dwErrorTableEnd address (table sentinel)\n  0x100155c4 - Error message string pointer offset in table entries\n  0x3c (60)  - Maximum module path length before truncation\n  0xfc (252) - No-op sentinel error code\n  0x12010    - MB_OK | MB_ICONERROR | MB_TASKMODAL flags\n  0xfffffff4 - STD_ERROR_HANDLE (-12)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
