      "name": "_strncnt",
      "signature": "size_t _strncnt(char * lpszString, size_t nMaxCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "size_t",
      "comment": "Counts characters in a string up to a maximum count or null terminator.\n\nThis is a CRT library function from Visual Studio 1998 Release that provides\nbounded string length counting, similar to strnlen but with different edge\ncase handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointer to start of string and remaining count\n2. If count is zero, skip directly to null-terminator check\n3. Loop: decrement remaining count, check for null terminator\n4. If null found or count exhausted, calculate length as pointer difference\n5. Return either the calculated length or original count (if string continues)\n\nParameters:\n  lpszString (char*): Pointer to null-terminated string to count\n  nMaxCount (size_t): Maximum number of characters to count\n\nReturns:\n  size_t: Number of characters counted, which is the lesser of:\n          - The position of the null terminator\n          - The maximum count (nMaxCount) if string is longer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nMaxCount is 0, returns 0 if first char is null, otherwise returns nMaxCount\n  - Empty string (lpszString[0] == '\\0') returns 0 regardless of nMaxCount\n\nCalled By: MapLocaleStringWithCodePage\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 1998 Release",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
