      "name": "ShowCrtMessageBox",
      "signature": "int ShowCrtMessageBox(LPCSTR lpszText, LPCSTR lpszCaption, UINT dwType)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Displays a CRT-safe message box by dynamically loading user32.dll.\n\nThis is a C Runtime (CRT) helper function from Visual Studio 1998 that ensures\nMessageBoxA can be called safely during CRT initialization or error handling\nwhen user32.dll may not yet be loaded.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if MessageBoxA function pointer is already cached\n2. If not cached, load user32.dll via LoadLibraryA\n3. Resolve MessageBoxA, GetActiveWindow, and GetLastActivePopup via GetProcAddress\n4. Cache the function pointers in global variables for subsequent calls\n5. Get the active window handle via GetActiveWindow\n6. Get the last active popup of that window via GetLastActivePopup\n7. Call MessageBoxA with the resolved parent window handle\n\nParameters:\n  lpszText    - LPCSTR: Message text to display in the message box\n  lpszCaption - LPCSTR: Caption text for the message box title bar\n  dwType      - UINT: Message box style flags (MB_OK, MB_YESNO, etc.)\n\nReturns:\n  int - MessageBoxA return value (IDOK, IDCANCEL, IDYES, IDNO, etc.)\n        Returns 0 if user32.dll or MessageBoxA cannot be loaded\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - First call performs DLL loading and function resolution\n  - Subsequent calls use cached function pointers for performance\n  - If GetActiveWindow returns NULL, MessageBoxA uses NULL as parent\n  - If GetLastActivePopup is unavailable, uses GetActiveWindow result directly",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
