      "name": "___crtGetStringTypeA",
      "signature": "BOOL ___crtGetStringTypeA(_locale_t pLocInfo, DWORD dwInfoType, LPCSTR lpszSrcStr, int nCchSrc, LPWORD pwCharType, int nCodePage, BOOL fError)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "BOOL",
      "comment": "CRT wrapper for GetStringTypeA/W that auto-detects OS string type API support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_nStringTypeApiMode cache (0=untested, 1=Unicode, 2=ANSI)\n2. If untested, probe GetStringTypeA first, then GetStringTypeW as fallback\n3. Cache result in g_nStringTypeApiMode for subsequent calls\n4. If ANSI mode (2): Call GetStringTypeA directly with code page\n5. If Unicode mode (1): Convert ANSI to Unicode via MultiByteToWideChar, then call GetStringTypeW\n6. Free allocated wide string buffer after Unicode path\n\nParameters:\n  pLocInfo    - Locale information structure (used for string type info)\n  dwInfoType  - Character type flags (CT_CTYPE1, CT_CTYPE2, CT_CTYPE3)\n  lpszSrcStr  - Source ANSI string to analyze\n  nCchSrc     - Character count of source string (-1 for null-terminated)\n  pwCharType  - Output buffer for character type results\n  nCodePage   - Code page for ANSI conversion (0 = use g_nAnsiCodePage)\n  fError      - Error handling flag\n\nReturns:\n  TRUE (non-zero) - Character type information retrieved successfully\n  FALSE (0)       - Failed to get string type (both API paths unavailable)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nCodePage is 0, uses g_nAnsiCodePage as fallback\n  - If pwCharType is NULL in Unicode path, uses g_dwDefaultCodePage\n  - First call probes both APIs to determine OS capabilities\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x9 - MB_ERR_INVALID_CHARS | MB_PRECOMPOSED for first MultiByteToWideChar call\n  0x1 - MB_PRECOMPOSED for second MultiByteToWideChar call\n  0x1 - CT_CTYPE1 for API availability test\n  0x2 - API mode: GetStringTypeA available\n  0x1 - API mode: GetStringTypeW available (Unicode)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
