      "name": "AllocateZeroedArrayMemory",
      "signature": "LPVOID AllocateZeroedArrayMemory(int nElementCount, int nElementSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "LPVOID",
      "comment": "Allocates zeroed memory for an array of elements using the private heap.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Multiply nElementCount by nElementSize to compute total allocation size\n  2. If computed size is zero, set minimum allocation to 1 byte\n  3. Validate size against maximum limit (0xffffffe1 bytes)\n  4. Call HeapAlloc with HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag (0x8) from g_hPrivateHeap\n  5. If allocation fails and g_dwMemAllocator handler exists, invoke it\n  6. Loop retry allocation until success or handler returns 0\n  7. Return pointer to allocated memory or NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\n  nElementCount - Number of elements to allocate (int)\n  nElementSize  - Size of each element in bytes (int)\n\nReturns:\n  LPVOID - Pointer to zero-initialized memory on success\n  NULL   - On allocation failure after handler exhaustion or size overflow\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero allocation: nElementCount * nElementSize = 0 results in 1 byte allocation\n  - Size overflow: Allocations > 0xffffffe1 bytes immediately fail\n  - Handler retry: If g_dwMemAllocator is set, InvokeOptionalHandler is called to\n    attempt memory recovery before retrying allocation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x8         - HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag for HeapAlloc\n  0xffffffe1  - Maximum allocation size limit (prevents overflow)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d87b6d24caec563811d284ff839eac090669dd28c7b37e269a01f99037d51262",
