      "name": "BuildHuffmanTreeWithEscapes",
      "signature": "void BuildHuffmanTreeWithEscapes(uint dwBitBuffer, int * pTreeOutput)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Builds a Huffman decoding tree with three escape code branches from a compressed bitstream.\n\nThis function constructs a binary tree structure for Huffman decoding that includes special\nhandling for three escape codes. Escape codes are 16-bit values read from the stream header\nthat mark positions in the tree requiring special branch handling during later decoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read 3 escape codes (16-bit each) from bitstream, store to globals at 0x10014be0-be4\n2. Initialize tree header: first DWORD=0, next three DWORDs for escape branch pointers\n3. Push sentinel values -1 (end marker) and -2 (continuation marker) onto stack\n4. Main decode loop: read 1 bit from stream\n   a. Bit=1: Push current position, advance tree cursor, continue loop\n   b. Bit=0: Pop stack state, decode symbol from two Huffman lookup tables\n5. Compare decoded 16-bit symbol against escape codes 1/2/3\n   a. Match escape1: Store current tree position at [EDX+0x4], set symbol=0\n   b. Match escape2: Store current tree position at [EDX+0x8], set symbol=0\n   c. Match escape3: Store current tree position at [EDX+0xC], set symbol=0\n6. Store leaf node: (symbol << 16) | 0x01 marks leaf with high bit clear\n7. Back-patch parent node with encoded child offset when returning from branch\n8. Loop until sentinel -1 popped (tree complete)\n9. Finalize: Set default branch pointers to current cursor if not already set\n\nParameters:\n  dwBitBuffer (ECX): Initial bit buffer value containing packed bits for decoding\n  pTreeOutput (EDX): Pointer to output tree structure (minimum 16 bytes header + tree nodes)\n  IMPLICIT ESI: Source data pointer, advanced by 4 bytes per DWORD consumed\n  IMPLICIT EDI: Tree output cursor, advanced by 4 bytes per node written\n  IMPLICIT EBP: Bit buffer register, shifted right as bits consumed\n\nReturns:\n  void - Tree written to pTreeOutput; ESI/EDI/EBP modified\n  pTreeOutput[0]: Always 0 (root marker)\n  pTreeOutput[1]: Pointer to escape branch 1 subtree (or default end position)\n  pTreeOutput[2]: Pointer to escape branch 2 subtree (or default end position)\n  pTreeOutput[3]: Pointer to escape branch 3 subtree (or default end position)\n\nGlobal References:\n  0x10014ac0: Bit counter (byte) - tracks remaining bits in buffer\n  0x10014a7c: Huffman table 1 pointer - high byte lookup\n  0x10014a80: Huffman table 2 pointer - low byte lookup\n  0x10014be0: Escape code 1 (word)\n  0x10014be2: Escape code 2 (word)\n  0x10014be4: Escape code 3 (word)\n\nTree Node Format:\n  Leaf node:   (symbol << 16) | 0x01  - high 16 bits = symbol, low bit = 1\n  Branch node: (offset << 13)         - encoded offset to child, low bits clear\n\nBit Buffer Protocol:\n  - Consumes 8 bits per byte read via SHR EBP,8\n  - Refills from [ESI] with 24-bit add when counter < 9\n  - Counter at 0x10014ac0 wraps at 32 bits (0x20)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
