      "name": "DecompressBitStreamData",
      "signature": "void DecompressBitStreamData(dword dwBitBuffer, int * pOutputData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decompresses bitstream-encoded data using bit-level bit extraction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Decrement global bit counter (g_byBitCount at 0x10014ac0) to extract next bit\n  2. If counter reaches zero (0x00), reload from next source dword at [ESI], reset to 0x20 (32)\n  3. Right-shift dwBitBuffer by 1 to extract LSB (carry flag set if bit was 1)\n  4. If LSB=0: zero pOutputData[0], set pOutputData[1-3] to EAX value, jump to return\n  5. If LSB=1: recursively read 3 more bits via DecompressBitstream calls\n  6. Call BuildHuffmanTreeWithEscapes to decode escape codes from bitstream\n  7. Call ProcessSearchPattern to finalize decompression\n  8. Return\n\nParameters:\n  ECX (dwBitBuffer): Starting bit buffer value (typically filled from source)\n  EDX (pOutputData): Pointer to 4-dword output array [0]=sentinel, [1-3]=data\n\nReturns:\n  void; results stored via pOutputData pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Bit buffer exhaustion during processing (automatic refill from global state)\n  Multiple decompression calls from parent (FUN_1000e530) with different output buffers\n  Global escape code caching (g_wEscapeCode1, g_wEscapeCode2, g_wEscapeCode3)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:63566c6fe24149ecedf51cd573706a00823db2c8c5b03ee14c0eaf3a60fe147d",
