      "name": "InitializeHuffmanDecodeTables",
      "signature": "void InitializeHuffmanDecodeTables(void * this, int * param_1, undefined4 * param_2, undefined4 param_3, undefined4 param_4, undefined4 param_5, undefined4 param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes Huffman decoding tables for Smacker video decompression.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store all input parameters to global storage locations for nested calls\n2. Initialize three Huffman table pointers at 0x800-byte offsets from pSmackContext\n3. Set default bit depth (12 bits) and table size (0x1000 entries) constants\n4. Call DecompressBitStreamData four times for each Huffman table section:\n   - Table 1: Base offset 0x10, full 0x1000 entries\n   - Table 2: Offset 0x4010, adds dwTableSize1\n   - Table 3: Offset 0x8010, adds dwTableSize1 + dwTableSize2\n   - Table 4: Offset 0xC010 (10-bit depth, 0x400 entries), adds sizes 1-3\n5. Copy table size parameters to output buffer header (first 4 DWORDs)\n6. Copy 0x10 DWORDs of table configuration data to output + 0xD014\n7. Zero-fill 0x800 DWORDs (0x2000 bytes) of Huffman table memory\n8. Call FUN_1000e880 four times for each table section (builds lookup tables)\n9. Perform bit scan (SCASD.REPE/BSF) to find maximum bit position in tables\n10. Call FUN_1000e8b0 four times to finalize table entries\n\nParameters:\n  pContext (ECX, IMPLICIT): Unused this pointer for __thiscall convention\n  pSmackContext: Pointer to Smacker decompression context (stores table pointers)\n  pHuffmanBuffer: Pre-allocated buffer for Huffman table storage (min 0x2000 bytes)\n  pOutputBuffer: Output buffer receiving decompressed table data and header\n  dwTableSize1: Size of first Huffman table section in bytes\n  dwTableSize2: Size of second Huffman table section in bytes\n  dwTableSize3: Size of third Huffman table section in bytes\n  dwTableSize4: Size of fourth Huffman table section in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; tables initialized in-place via pOutputBuffer\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  - 0x10015030: Stores pSmackContext\n  - 0x10015034: Stores pOutputBuffer\n  - 0x10015038-0x10015044: Stores dwTableSize1-4\n  - 0x10014A00-0x10014A30: Table configuration structures (0x10 bytes each)\n  - 0x10014AB0: Bit depth setting (12 or 10 bits)\n  - 0x10014AB4: Table size setting (0x1000 or 0x400 entries)\n  - 0x10014AD0: Maximum bit position result\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0x800: Offset between Huffman table sections (2048 bytes)\n  - 0xD068: Offset to compressed bit stream in output buffer\n  - 0xD014: Offset to table configuration in output buffer\n  - 0x1000: Default table entry count (4096)\n  - 0x400: Reduced table entry count for table 4 (1024)\n  - 0xC/0xA: Bit depth values (12-bit and 10-bit)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
