      "name": "DecodeSmackerFrame",
      "signature": "ulonglong DecodeSmackerFrame(uint dwReserved1, uint dwReserved2, uint * pBitstream, byte * pHuffmanBuffer, byte * pFrameInfo)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "ulonglong",
      "comment": "Decodes a single Smacker video frame using Huffman decompression.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store buffer base pointer and initialize Huffman lookup tables\n2. Copy 16 entries (4 iterations x 4 entries) from buffer+0xD014 to g_HuffmanTable1Data\n3. Setup 4 Huffman tree pointers at offsets 0x10, 0x4010, 0x8010, 0xC010\n4. Parse frame flags from pFrameInfo:\n   - Byte 0, bit 0: Streaming mode (inverted - 0=streaming, 1=non-streaming)\n   - Byte 2, bit 7: Double-Y mode (interlaced scaling)\n   - Byte 1, bit 0: Interlaced mode\n5. Select appropriate decode handler table based on mode flags\n6. For non-streaming mode: Extract frame dimensions from pFrameInfo+0x8 through +0x1C\n7. For streaming mode: Process command stream with special codes:\n   - 0xFFFD: Call stream callback\n   - 0xFFFE: Update frame parameters\n   - 0xFFFF: End of stream\n8. Detect CPU SIMD capabilities (MMX vs non-MMX)\n9. Initialize decode entry points based on SIMD level:\n   - Level < 2: Use non-SIMD handlers at 0x1000E8E0, 0x1000E9E0, 0x1000EB90\n   - Level >= 2: Use MMX handlers at 0x1000ED40, 0x1000EE40, 0x1000F010\n10. Begin Huffman bit-stream decoding via jump table dispatch\n\nParameters:\n  dwReserved1 (ECX) - Reserved, not used by function\n  dwReserved2 (EDX) - Reserved, not used by function\n  pBitstream - Pointer to compressed bitstream data\n  pHuffmanBuffer - Base address of Huffman decode buffer (size 0xD054)\n  pFrameInfo - Pointer to frame descriptor structure\n\nReturns:\n  Low 32 bits: Pointer to output buffer or decode result\n  High 32 bits: Additional state (varies by decode path)\n\nFrame Info Structure Layout (pFrameInfo):\n  Offset|Size|Field|Type|Description\n  0x00|1|bFlags0|byte|Bit 0: streaming mode (inverted)\n  0x01|1|bFlags1|byte|Bit 0: interlaced mode\n  0x02|1|bFlags2|byte|Bit 7: double-Y scaling mode\n  0x04|4|pfnCallback|ptr|Stream callback function (streaming mode)\n  0x08|4|dwWidth|dword|Frame width in pixels\n  0x0C|4|dwHeight|dword|Frame height in pixels\n  0x10|4|dwStride|dword|Row stride in bytes\n  0x14|4|dwPadLeft|dword|Left padding amount\n  0x18|4|dwBlocks|dword|Number of 4x4 blocks\n  0x1C|4|dwPadRight|dword|Right padding amount\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early at LAB_10011ed0 for streaming mode end-of-stream\n  - Non-SIMD path uses 32-bit register operations\n  - MMX path uses 64-bit MOVQ for bitstream reads",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
