      "name": "DecompressSmackFrame",
      "signature": "void DecompressSmackFrame(dword * pBitstream, int nFrameType, dword * pHuffTable1, dword * pHuffTable2, dword * pOutputStart, dword * pOutputCurrent)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decompresses a single Smack frame using Huffman decoding\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize global bitstream state from input parameters\n  2. Read frame type bits (bits 0-2) to determine decompression mode:\n     - Mode 0 (0x1): 8-bit greyscale data with single Huffman tree\n     - Mode 1 (0x3): 16-bit data with two independent Huffman trees\n     - Mode 2 (0x5): 16-bit data with predicate-based Huffman selection\n     - Mode 3 (0x7): 32-bit RGBA data with four Huffman trees\n  3. Build or decompress Huffman trees as specified by frame type\n  4. For each output byte/word/dword:\n     - Refill bitstream cache when bits exhausted (0x20 bits = 32 bits)\n     - Traverse Huffman tree using bitstream bits\n     - Combine decoded values into output element\n  5. Handle output buffer wrapping at boundary (pOutputStart/pOutputCurrent)\n\nParameters:\n  pBitstream    - Pointer to dword array of encoded bitstream data\n  nFrameType    - Frame type code (determines decoding mode and Huffman setup)\n  pHuffTable1   - Pointer to primary Huffman tree array\n  pHuffTable2   - Pointer to secondary Huffman tree array (used in multi-tree modes)\n  pOutputStart  - Pointer to output buffer start (for wrap-around calculations)\n  pOutputCurrent - Pointer to current output position in buffer\n\nReturns:\n  None (output written to memory at pOutputCurrent and beyond)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Wraps output at pOutputStart boundary (circular buffer)\n  - Handles sub-byte bit alignment with cache management\n  - Supports 8, 16, and 32-bit output element sizes based on frame type\n  - Requires global state variables: g_byBitCount, g_pHuffmanTable1, g_pHuffmanTable2",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
