      "name": "CalcSmackerBufferOffset",
      "signature": "dword CalcSmackerBufferOffset(dword dwContext, dword dwBase, int nWidth, int nHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Calculates scaled buffer offset for pixel/video processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Multiply nWidth * nHeight to get pixel/frame size\n  2. Shift right by 8 bits (divide by 256) to scale the value\n  3. Add 0x20 (32) as padding or header offset\n  4. Return combined 64-bit value with dwBase\n\nParameters:\n  dwContext: Context value passed in ECX (purpose unclear)\n  dwBase: Base address/context value passed in EDX\n  nWidth: Width dimension value on stack\n  nHeight: Height dimension value on stack\n\nReturns:\n  EDX:EAX - 64-bit result with dwBase in EDX and calculated offset in EAX\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Product overflow: If nWidth*nHeight exceeds 2^32, only lower 32 bits used\n  Right shift handles large values by reducing magnitude",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:7c3390f6b9178d78f90664be2437ec0249af03dee5cbdc9bc711f8531cc624ad",
