      "name": "SmackDecompressNextBlock",
      "signature": "dword SmackDecompressNextBlock(dword dwReserved1, dword dwReserved2, int pSmackBuffer, dword * pOutputRect)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Decompresses next block from a Smack-compressed buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if initial flush flag (offset +0x20) is set\n  2. If not set, initialize decompression state from structure fields\n  3. Process input bit stream at current bit position (offset +0x2C)\n  4. Output decompressed data at current output index (offset +0x30)\n  5. Handle block boundary conditions (0x40 byte alignment)\n  6. Update state flags and positions for next block\n  7. Return 1 on success, 0 on completion\n\nParameters:\n  dwReserved1 [ECX]:    Reserved/unused parameter\n  dwReserved2 [EDX]:    Reserved/unused parameter\n  pSmackBuffer [ESP+4]: Pointer to Smack decompression state structure\n  pOutputRect [ESP+8]:  Pointer to output rectangle array (4 dwords)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 1: Block decompressed successfully, more blocks remain\n  EAX = 0: Decompression complete or buffer exhausted\n\nStructure Layout (pSmackBuffer):\n  Offset | Size | Field                | Description\n  0x20   | 1    | bFlushFlag           | Initial setup complete flag\n  0x21   | 1    | bMidBlockFlag        | Mid-block continuation flag\n  0x22   | 1    | bInitFlag            | Initialization flag\n  0x24   | 4    | dwMaxBitPosition     | Maximum bit position (stream length)\n  0x28   | 4    | dwMaxOutputIndex     | Maximum output index\n  0x2C   | 4    | dwBitPosition        | Current bit position\n  0x30   | 4    | dwOutputIndex        | Current output position\n  0x34   | 4    | pInputPointer        | Current input byte pointer\n  0x38   | 4    | pInputBase           | Base of input buffer\n\nOutput Array (pOutputRect):\n  [0]: dwBitPosition (X coordinate)\n  [1]: dwOutputIndex (Y coordinate)\n  [2]: dwBlockSize   (Width/size)\n  [3]: 0x4           (Height/constant)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
