      "name": "ConvertRgb24ToRgb555",
      "signature": "void ConvertRgb24ToRgb555(ushort * pDest555, byte * pSrc24)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts 256 RGB24 (24-bit) pixels to RGB555 (15-bit) format for Smacker video.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Loop 0x100 (256) iterations\n  2. Read 32-bit value at pSrc24 (includes extra byte due to alignment)\n  3. Extract high word wHighWord = dwSrcPixel >> 16 (contains B component)\n  4. Advance source pointer by 3 bytes (RGB24 stride)\n  5. Extract and pack color components:\n     - R: bits 7:3 of byte 0 -> bits 14:10 of output\n     - G: bits 7:3 of byte 1 -> bits 9:5 of output  \n     - B: bits 7:3 of byte 2 -> bits 4:0 of output\n  6. Mask result to 0x7FFF (15-bit RGB555)\n  7. Write 16-bit output pixel\n  8. Advance destination pointer by 2 bytes\n\nParameters:\n  pDest555 - Pointer to destination buffer for RGB555 pixels (512 bytes min)\n  pSrc24 - Pointer to source buffer of RGB24 pixels (768 bytes min)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies pDest555 buffer in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Fixed pixel count of 0x100 (256) pixels\n  - Source reads 3 bytes per pixel (RGB24 packed)\n  - Destination writes 2 bytes per pixel (RGB555 packed)\n  - No bounds checking performed\n  - Used by Smack video decoder during frame blit operations",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:ca2bb58dcc85754bd542b8ae159254a6c09fafd15e73390f7f9f62a01f415c06",
