      "name": "DecodeHuffmanSymbol",
      "signature": "void DecodeHuffmanSymbol(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decodes the next Huffman symbol from the Smacker bitstream and dispatches to appropriate handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if bit buffer needs refilling (AL <= 10 bits remaining)\n2. If low on bits, read 16-bit word from ESI stream, shift into EBP accumulator\n3. Extract 10-bit index from bit accumulator (AND 0x3FF) for Huffman table lookup\n4. Look up Huffman node via g_pHuffmanTable[index], extract code length from low byte\n5. Shift accumulator right by code length, subtract from bit count\n6. Extract symbol offset from high bytes, add to g_dwBufferBasePtr\n7. Compare current symbol (BX) with table entry (DX) - if match, traverse tree\n8. On tree traversal: test next bit (SHR/JC), select left (offset 4) or right child\n9. When final symbol found, rotate to extract handler index and block data\n10. Update Huffman node cache (g_pLastHuffmanNode swap buffers for LRU)\n11. Extract handler index (AND 0x3) and block lookup (AND 0xFC)\n12. Store block data to g_dwCurrentBlockData, jump to handler via g_apfnDecodeHandlers\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT ESI - Pointer to input bitstream buffer (advanced during execution)\n  IMPLICIT EBP - 32-bit bit accumulator containing pending bits\n  IMPLICIT EBX - Previous symbol value for tree comparison\n  IMPLICIT AL  - Current bit count in accumulator (0-32)\n  (Note: All parameters passed via registers, no stack parameters)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function does not return normally; dispatches to handler via jump table\n  Side Effects:\n    - ESI advanced by 2 or 4 bytes depending on refill needs\n    - EBP updated with remaining bits after symbol extraction\n    - AL updated with remaining bit count\n    - g_byBitCount updated with final bit count\n    - g_dwCurrentBlockData set with block type data for handler\n    - g_pLastHuffmanNode LRU cache updated if node changed\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_byBitCount (0x10014ac0)      - Remaining bits in accumulator (byte)\n  g_pHuffmanTable (0x100149fc)   - 10-bit indexed Huffman lookup table\n  g_dwBufferBasePtr (0x10014a94) - Base pointer for symbol buffer\n  g_pLastHuffmanNode (0x10014a34) - Last accessed Huffman node (cache)\n  g_pHuffmanSwapBuffer1/2        - LRU swap buffers for node caching\n  g_apfnDecodeHandlers (0x10014a40) - Jump table for decode handlers [4 entries]\n  g_aBlockLookupTable (0x10014ae0)  - Block type lookup table\n  g_dwCurrentBlockData (0x10014a54) - Current block data for handler\n\nHuffman Table Entry Format:\n  Bits 0-7:   Code length (bits to consume)\n  Bits 8-15:  Symbol offset low byte\n  Bits 16-31: Symbol data (rotated for extraction)\n\nHandler Dispatch:\n  Index 0-3 selects handler from g_apfnDecodeHandlers\n  Implements Smacker's 4 block types: mono, full, void, solid",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
